 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingnessMechanism|skos:scopeNote"
 msgid "Declares a missingness assumption, distinct from math:hasMissingnessIndicator recording absence, math:missingDataPolicy describing supplied analysis handling, and an event-specific target strategy named through math:intercurrentEventHandling. An assumption is not itself a handling procedure."
 msgstr "Déclare une hypothèse de manque, distincte de math:hasMissingnessIndicator qui consigne l’absence, de math:missingDataPolicy qui décrit le traitement analytique fourni et d’une stratégie cible propre à un événement nommée par math:intercurrentEventHandling. Une hypothèse n’est pas elle-même une procédure de traitement."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RatioQuantity|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Ratio quantity"
+msgstr "Quantité de rapport"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RatioQuantity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A quantity interpreted in a quotient reference frame with explicit numerator and denominator frames. Its magnitude uses math:quantityValue and its dimension uses math:hasDimension; frame composition preserves the two unit contexts rather than making every dimensionless ratio interchangeable. This quantity form is distinct from the integer representation of math:RationalValue."
+msgstr "Une quantité interprétée dans un référentiel quotient dont les référentiels du numérateur et du dénominateur sont explicites. Sa grandeur utilise math:quantityValue et sa dimension math:hasDimension ; la composition des référentiels conserve les deux contextes d’unité sans rendre tous les rapports sans dimension interchangeables. Cette forme de quantité est distincte de la représentation entière de math:RationalValue."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuotientReferenceFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Quotient reference frame"
+msgstr "Référentiel quotient"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuotientReferenceFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A reference frame whose unit interpretation is one explicitly identified numerator frame per one explicitly identified denominator frame. It retains the ordinary reference-frame profile and both component identities. This structural composition supplies no implicit scale factor, currency conversion, frame equivalence or general quotient evaluator."
+msgstr "Un référentiel dont l’interprétation d’unité est un référentiel numérateur explicitement identifié par un référentiel dénominateur explicitement identifié. Il conserve le profil ordinaire d’un référentiel et les deux identités composantes. Cette composition structurelle ne fournit aucun facteur d’échelle implicite, conversion monétaire, équivalence de référentiels ni évaluateur général de quotient."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numeratorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "numerator frame"
+msgstr "référentiel du numérateur"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numeratorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The numerator reference frame of a math:QuotientReferenceFrame. For a selected unit-price quantity this is the currency frame, not a monetary amount or a numeric numerator."
+msgstr "Le référentiel du numérateur d’un math:QuotientReferenceFrame. Pour une quantité de prix unitaire sélectionnée, il s’agit du référentiel monétaire, non d’un montant monétaire ni d’un numérateur numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/denominatorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "denominator frame"
+msgstr "référentiel du dénominateur"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/denominatorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The denominator reference frame of a math:QuotientReferenceFrame. For a selected unit-price quantity this identifies the counted-unit frame; equality of physical dimensions alone does not identify that frame."
+msgstr "Le référentiel du dénominateur d’un math:QuotientReferenceFrame. Pour une quantité de prix unitaire sélectionnée, il identifie le référentiel de l’unité comptée ; l’égalité des dimensions physiques ne suffit pas à identifier ce référentiel."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteRatioFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Incomplete ratio frame"
+msgstr "Référentiel de rapport incomplet"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteRatioFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A conformance failure in which a RatioQuantity lacks its unique quotient reference frame or a QuotientReferenceFrame lacks a unique, correctly typed numerator or denominator frame. It identifies missing or conflicting structure, not a failed numerical division."
+msgstr "Un échec de conformité où une RatioQuantity ne possède pas son unique référentiel quotient, ou où un QuotientReferenceFrame ne possède pas un référentiel numérateur ou dénominateur unique et correctement typé. Il identifie une structure absente ou contradictoire, non une division numérique échouée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecRatioQuantityFramed|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "A dimensioned RatioQuantity declares one QuotientReferenceFrame with one typed numerator and denominator frame. Its complete component contexts remain distinct and no arithmetic result is asserted."
+msgstr "Une RatioQuantity dimensionnée déclare un QuotientReferenceFrame avec un référentiel typé au numérateur et un au dénominateur. Les contextes complets des composants demeurent distincts et aucun résultat arithmétique n’est affirmé."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecRatioQuantityMissingFrame|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The framed control with only the RatioQuantity hasReferenceFrame edge removed must raise IncompleteRatioFrame from the canonical closed required path. Its dimension and the unused complete quotient remain valid."
+msgstr "Le témoin avec référentiel dont seule l’arête hasReferenceFrame de RatioQuantity a été retirée doit produire IncompleteRatioFrame à partir du chemin requis fermé canonique. Sa dimension et le quotient complet inutilisé restent valides."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecQuotientFrameMissingDenominator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The framed control with only denominatorFrame removed must raise IncompleteRatioFrame from the quotient's closed required denominator path. The numerator, quantity frame and ordinary reference profiles remain supplied."
+msgstr "Le témoin avec référentiel dont seul denominatorFrame a été retiré doit produire IncompleteRatioFrame à partir du chemin fermé du dénominateur requis du quotient. Le numérateur, le référentiel de la quantité et les profils de référence ordinaires restent fournis."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Basis"
+msgstr "Base"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "An algebraic basis of a vector space over its scalar field: a linearly independent spanning family. Every vector has unique finitely supported coefficients indexed by the basis elements. The basis is distinct from an ordering of its elements, a coordinate array and an inner product."
+msgstr "Une base algébrique d’un espace vectoriel sur son corps des scalaires : une famille libre et génératrice. Chaque vecteur possède des coefficients uniques à support fini, indexés par les éléments de la base. La base est distincte d’un ordre sur ses éléments, d’un tableau de coordonnées et d’un produit scalaire."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Uniqueness is relative to the vector space and scalar field. Indexed coefficients need not form an ordered tuple; positional coordinates additionally require a correspondence between positions and basis elements. A named Basis record alone does not establish independence or spanning."
+msgstr "L’unicité est relative à l’espace vectoriel et au corps des scalaires. Des coefficients indexés ne forment pas nécessairement un tuple ordonné ; des coordonnées positionnelles exigent en plus une correspondance entre positions et éléments de la base. Un enregistrement Basis nommé ne suffit pas à établir que la famille est libre ou génératrice."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer declares p:covBasis as math:Basis and links its Gram matrix to that resource through math:inBasis. The RDF names the context but does not enumerate basis elements or their order."
+msgstr "Le producteur exact-pca déclare p:covBasis comme math:Basis et relie sa matrice de Gram à cette ressource par math:inBasis. Le RDF nomme le contexte sans énumérer les éléments de la base ni leur ordre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to name a supplied basis underlying vectors, coordinate arrays or an algebra carrier, retaining the actual vector space and scalar field."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour nommer une base fournie pour des vecteurs, des tableaux de coordonnées ou le support d’une algèbre, en conservant l’espace vectoriel et le corps des scalaires effectifs."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer orthonormality or eigenvector roles from the Basis type. A self-adjoint operator on a finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product space admits an orthonormal eigenbasis; not every basis is an eigenbasis. Do not extend that conclusion to arbitrary infinite-dimensional self-adjoint operators or assume that truncated PCA components span the full input space."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire l’orthonormalité ni un rôle de vecteur propre du type Basis. Un opérateur autoadjoint sur un espace préhilbertien réel ou complexe de dimension finie admet une base orthonormée de vecteurs propres ; toute base n’est pas une telle base. Ne pas étendre cette conclusion aux opérateurs autoadjoints arbitraires en dimension infinie ni supposer que des composantes principales tronquées engendrent tout l’espace d’entrée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the basis as its own resource. Use math:hasBasis on the supplied space or algebra and math:inBasis on a vector or Gram matrix. Preserve any supplied element inventory and ordering evidence; neither link constructs a basis or computes a coordinate transform."
+msgstr "Décrire la base comme une ressource distincte. Utiliser math:hasBasis sur l’espace ou l’algèbre fournis et math:inBasis sur un vecteur ou une matrice de Gram. Conserver tout inventaire d’éléments et toute preuve d’ordre fournis ; aucun de ces liens ne construit une base ni ne calcule une transformation de coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "In the finite real Cl(p,q) profile, the algebra carrier has dimension 2^(p+q), while there are p+q grade-one generators. The producer emits selected generator records through math:hasBasisBlade; those records do not enumerate the complete carrier basis or prove independence and spanning."
+msgstr "Dans le profil réel fini Cl(p,q), le support de l’algèbre a pour dimension 2^(p+q), alors qu’il existe p+q générateurs de grade un. Le producteur émet des enregistrements de générateurs sélectionnés par math:hasBasisBlade ; ils n’énumèrent pas la base complète du support et ne prouvent pas que ses éléments sont libres et générateurs."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The Clifford producer names a separate BladeBasis through math:hasBasis and emits grade-one math:BasisBlade records with math:generatorIndex. The named carrier basis and the indexed generator records retain different roles."
+msgstr "Le producteur Clifford nomme une BladeBasis distincte par math:hasBasis et émet des enregistrements math:BasisBlade de grade un avec math:generatorIndex. La base nommée du support et les enregistrements de générateurs indexés conservent des rôles distincts."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to record an actual basis choice for a vector space, quadratic space or algebra carrier, including several supplied choices without selecting a preferred basis."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour consigner un choix effectif de base pour un espace vectoriel, un espace quadratique ou le support d’une algèbre, y compris plusieurs choix fournis sans sélectionner une base préférée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not count the emitted grade-one generator records as the full algebra carrier basis or treat generator order as a complete blade-basis order. A hasBasis link alone does not prove linear independence or spanning and does not choose an unrecorded default."
+msgstr "Ne pas compter les enregistrements émis de générateurs de grade un comme la base complète du support de l’algèbre, ni traiter l’ordre des générateurs comme un ordre complet de base de lames. Un lien hasBasis seul ne prouve pas que la famille est libre et génératrice et ne choisit aucune base par défaut non consignée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the supplied space or algebra to its Basis resource with math:hasBasis. Retain the CliffordAlgebra class-local requirement for a typed basis without making this property globally functional. Record supplied generator indices separately and use math:inBasis for coordinate representations."
+msgstr "Relier l’espace ou l’algèbre fournis à leur ressource Basis par math:hasBasis. Conserver l’exigence locale à la classe CliffordAlgebra d’une base typée sans rendre cette propriété globalement fonctionnelle. Consigner séparément les indices de générateurs fournis et utiliser math:inBasis pour les représentations en coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "in basis"
+msgstr "dans la base"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:GramMatrix or math:Vector to the math:Basis relative to which its entries or coordinates are recorded. The link identifies the declared basis context; it does not supply the element inventory, its order or a coordinate transformation."
+msgstr "Relie une math:GramMatrix ou un math:Vector à la math:Basis relativement à laquelle ses entrées ou coordonnées sont consignées. Le lien identifie le contexte de base déclaré ; il ne fournit ni l’inventaire des éléments, ni leur ordre, ni une transformation de coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Matrix row/column indices and vector component indices are positions. Interpreting them as basis elements additionally requires the supplied position-to-element correspondence. The exact producer names p:covBasis only as Basis, so its inBasis edge alone does not publish such an ordered inventory."
+msgstr "Les indices de ligne et de colonne d’une matrice et les indices de composantes d’un vecteur sont des positions. Leur interprétation comme éléments d’une base exige en plus la correspondance fournie entre positions et éléments. Le producteur exact nomme p:covBasis uniquement comme Basis ; son arête inBasis ne publie donc pas à elle seule un tel inventaire ordonné."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:pcaGram math:inBasis p:covBasis and separately p:pcaGram math:representsForm p:covForm. These identify the coordinate context and represented form, without enumerating the basis elements or their order."
+msgstr "Le producteur exact-pca émet p:pcaGram math:inBasis p:covBasis et, séparément, p:pcaGram math:representsForm p:covForm. Ces liens identifient le contexte de coordonnées et la forme représentée, sans énumérer les éléments de la base ni leur ordre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to preserve the actual basis context of supplied Gram-matrix entries or vector coordinates, separately from the coordinate-independent vector or bilinear form."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver le contexte de base effectif des entrées de matrice de Gram ou des coordonnées de vecteur fournies, séparément du vecteur ou de la forme bilinéaire indépendants des coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat a basis label or inBasis link as proof that an indexed array is complete, correctly ordered or expressed in that basis. Changing the link alone does not transform the entries, and no conversion between differently based arrays is implicit."
+msgstr "Ne pas considérer un libellé de base ou un lien inBasis comme une preuve qu’un tableau indexé est complet, correctement ordonné ou exprimé dans cette base. Modifier le lien seul ne transforme pas les entrées et aucune conversion entre tableaux exprimés dans des bases différentes n’est implicite."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Attach math:inBasis to the supplied vector or Gram matrix and retain any explicit basis-element ordering with its indexed components or entries. Keep math:representsForm separate from the coordinate context. A basis change needs an actual transformation and its inputs; this relation records no such execution."
+msgstr "Attacher math:inBasis au vecteur ou à la matrice de Gram fournis et conserver tout ordre explicite des éléments de base avec les composantes ou entrées indexées. Séparer math:representsForm du contexte de coordonnées. Un changement de base exige une transformation effective et ses entrées ; cette relation ne consigne aucune exécution de ce type."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Eigendecomposition"
+msgstr "Décomposition en éléments propres"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A decomposition of a linear operator into eigenvalue and nonzero eigenvector data. In finite dimension, the diagonalization A = QΛQ⁻¹ requires a complete eigenbasis: Q is invertible, its columns are eigenvectors, and the diagonal entries of Λ are their eigenvalues in matching order."
+msgstr "Une décomposition d’un opérateur linéaire en données de valeurs propres et de vecteurs propres non nuls. En dimension finie, la diagonalisation A = QΛQ⁻¹ exige une base complète de vecteurs propres : Q est inversible, ses colonnes sont des vecteurs propres et les entrées diagonales de Λ sont leurs valeurs propres dans l’ordre correspondant."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The operator acts on the declared vector space over its scalar field; any extension of scalars is explicit. Not every operator is diagonalizable. Orthonormal or unitary eigenbasis claims require additional inner-product and operator hypotheses; the finite-dimensional formula does not assert an eigenvector basis for arbitrary infinite-dimensional operators."
+msgstr "L’opérateur agit sur l’espace vectoriel déclaré sur son corps des scalaires ; toute extension des scalaires est explicite. Tout opérateur n’est pas diagonalisable. Les affirmations de base propre orthonormée ou unitaire exigent des hypothèses supplémentaires sur le produit scalaire et l’opérateur ; la formule en dimension finie n’affirme pas l’existence d’une base propre pour des opérateurs arbitraires en dimension infinie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For A = diag(0,3) over the real numbers in a supplied ordered basis, Q = I and Λ = diag(0,3) give a complete diagonalization. Q is invertible although A is singular; the zero eigenvalue has the nonzero eigenvector (1,0)."
+msgstr "Pour A = diag(0,3) sur les réels dans une base ordonnée fournie, Q = I et Λ = diag(0,3) donnent une diagonalisation complète. Q est inversible bien que A soit singulière ; la valeur propre nulle a pour vecteur propre non nul (1,0)."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe supplied eigenvalue and eigenvector data for an operator, retaining the operator, vector space, scalar field and evidence for any claimed complete diagonalization."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour décrire des données fournies de valeurs propres et de vecteurs propres d’un opérateur, en conservant l’opérateur, l’espace vectoriel, le corps des scalaires et les éléments qui justifient toute diagonalisation complète revendiquée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer pairing, order, multiplicity or completeness from separate unordered math:eigenvalue and math:eigenvector links. Equal output counts, distinct node identities or repeated RDF assertions do not establish these facts, and the two output sets do not imply a Cartesian product of valid eigenpairs."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire l’appariement, l’ordre, la multiplicité ou la complétude de liens math:eigenvalue et math:eigenvector distincts et non ordonnés. Des nombres égaux de sorties, des identités de nœuds distinctes ou des assertions RDF répétées n’établissent pas ces faits, et les deux ensembles de sorties n’impliquent pas un produit cartésien de couples propres valides."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain actual source associations and ordering in their supplied representation. The registered skos:closeMatch to wd:Q190524 has logic:ValidationOnly preservation; it neither supplies an OpenMath eigen correspondence nor certifies numerical execution. A type or eigensolver descriptor alone proves no result."
+msgstr "Conserver les associations et l’ordre effectifs de la source dans leur représentation fournie. Le skos:closeMatch enregistré vers wd:Q190524 a pour préservation logic:ValidationOnly ; il ne fournit aucune correspondance OpenMath relative aux éléments propres et ne certifie aucune exécution numérique. Un type ou un descripteur de solveur de valeurs propres seul ne prouve aucun résultat."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "eigenvalue"
+msgstr "valeur propre"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Eigendecomposition to a math:Number representing a scalar λ for which Av = λv holds for some nonzero vector v in the declared vector space. The scalar belongs to the declared field, which may be real or complex; the number is a resource rather than a bare literal."
+msgstr "Relie une math:Eigendecomposition à un math:Number représentant un scalaire λ tel que Av = λv pour un vecteur non nul v de l’espace vectoriel déclaré. Le scalaire appartient au corps déclaré, qui peut être réel ou complexe ; le nombre est une ressource plutôt qu’un simple littéral."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Zero is a valid eigenvalue. In finite dimension, algebraic multiplicity counts a root of the characteristic polynomial, while geometric multiplicity is the dimension of its eigenspace. Neither is a count of distinct RDF number resources, and repeated identical RDF edges do not record multiplicity."
+msgstr "Zéro est une valeur propre valide. En dimension finie, la multiplicité algébrique est celle d’une racine du polynôme caractéristique, tandis que la multiplicité géométrique est la dimension de son sous-espace propre. Aucune ne compte les ressources numériques RDF distinctes, et la répétition d’arêtes RDF identiques ne consigne pas la multiplicité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real matrix A = diag(0,3), λ = 0 is an eigenvalue associated with v = (1,0). A math:eigenvalue link to the number resource records the scalar output; its association with this vector still needs the supplied source evidence."
+msgstr "Pour la matrice réelle A = diag(0,3), λ = 0 est une valeur propre associée à v = (1,0). Un lien math:eigenvalue vers la ressource numérique consigne la sortie scalaire ; son association à ce vecteur exige encore les éléments fournis par la source."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied eigenvalue as a number resource with its exact or approximate representation and the operator and scalar-field context of the decomposition."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver une valeur propre fournie comme ressource numérique avec sa représentation exacte ou approchée et le contexte d’opérateur et de corps des scalaires de la décomposition."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reject λ = 0, assume every real operator has real eigenvalues, or silently extend the scalar field. Do not pair this output with every math:eigenvector output or infer pairings from equal counts or RDF order."
+msgstr "Ne pas rejeter λ = 0, supposer que tout opérateur réel a des valeurs propres réelles ni étendre silencieusement le corps des scalaires. Ne pas apparier cette sortie avec chaque sortie math:eigenvector ni déduire des appariements de nombres égaux ou de l’ordre RDF."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied math:Number. Preserve its numeric representation and any source association, ordering and multiplicity evidence separately; this property alone supplies none of them and performs no eigensolver computation."
+msgstr "Relier la décomposition au math:Number fourni. Conserver séparément sa représentation numérique et tout élément de source établissant l’association, l’ordre et la multiplicité ; cette propriété seule ne les fournit pas et n’effectue aucun calcul de valeurs propres."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "eigenvector"
+msgstr "vecteur propre"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Eigendecomposition to a nonzero vector v satisfying Av = λv for an associated scalar λ, relative to the declared operator, vector space and scalar field. The vector is a mathematical object; its coordinates additionally depend on the supplied basis."
+msgstr "Relie une math:Eigendecomposition à un vecteur non nul v satisfaisant Av = λv pour un scalaire associé λ, relativement à l’opérateur, à l’espace vectoriel et au corps des scalaires déclarés. Le vecteur est un objet mathématique ; ses coordonnées dépendent en plus de la base fournie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "A nonzero scalar multiple remains an eigenvector for the same eigenvalue. Normalization and choice of representatives are additional data. Several independent vectors may share an eigenvalue, and a list of output resources alone establishes neither their independence nor the dimension of that eigenspace."
+msgstr "Un multiple scalaire non nul reste un vecteur propre pour la même valeur propre. La normalisation et le choix de représentants sont des données supplémentaires. Plusieurs vecteurs indépendants peuvent partager une valeur propre, et une liste de ressources de sortie seule n’établit ni leur indépendance ni la dimension du sous-espace propre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real matrix A = diag(0,3), v = (1,0) is a nonzero eigenvector with λ = 0, and 2v is another representative of the same eigendirection. The zero vector satisfies the equation but is not an eigenvector."
+msgstr "Pour la matrice réelle A = diag(0,3), v = (1,0) est un vecteur propre non nul de valeur propre λ = 0, et 2v est un autre représentant de la même direction propre. Le vecteur nul satisfait l’équation mais n’est pas un vecteur propre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied nonzero eigenvector output with its vector-space and scalar-field context, preserving any coordinate basis and actual source association to its eigenvalue."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver une sortie fournie de vecteur propre non nul avec son contexte d’espace vectoriel et de corps des scalaires, en préservant toute base de coordonnées et toute association effective de source à sa valeur propre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat the zero vector as an eigenvector or infer unit norm, orthogonality, a complete eigenbasis or an eigenvalue pairing from this link. A selected or truncated component family need not span the input space."
+msgstr "Ne pas traiter le vecteur nul comme un vecteur propre ni déduire de ce lien une norme unité, l’orthogonalité, une base propre complète ou un appariement à une valeur propre. Une famille de composantes sélectionnée ou tronquée n’engendre pas nécessairement l’espace d’entrée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied vector resource and retain its coordinates, basis, normalization and association evidence as provided. Keep eigenvalue associations explicit in the source representation; separate unordered output links neither construct eigenpairs nor execute a solver."
+msgstr "Relier la décomposition à la ressource vectorielle fournie et conserver ses coordonnées, sa base, sa normalisation et les éléments d’association tels qu’ils sont fournis. Garder les associations aux valeurs propres explicites dans la représentation de la source ; des liens de sortie distincts et non ordonnés ne construisent aucun couple propre et n’exécutent aucun solveur."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Singular Value Decomposition"
+msgstr "Décomposition en valeurs singulières"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A factorization of a linear map between finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product spaces. In orthonormal coordinates A = UΣV*, with orthonormal factor columns appropriate to the declared form, nonnegative real diagonal entries in Σ and V* the conjugate transpose (ordinary transpose over the reals)."
+msgstr "Une factorisation d’une application linéaire entre espaces préhilbertiens réels ou complexes de dimension finie. En coordonnées orthonormées, A = UΣV*, avec des colonnes de facteurs orthonormées adaptées à la forme déclarée, des entrées diagonales réelles non négatives dans Σ et V* la transposée conjuguée (la transposée ordinaire sur les réels)."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For m×n A, a full form has U m×m, Σ m×n and V n×n; a thin form may use k = min(m,n) columns, retaining zeros. A compact rank-r form retains the r positive singular-value occurrences. Names vary: retain supplied dimensions and zero treatment. Rectangular and singular maps are admitted; no eigenbasis or inverse is required."
+msgstr "Pour A de taille m×n, une forme complète a U de taille m×m, Σ de taille m×n et V de taille n×n ; une forme mince peut utiliser k = min(m,n) colonnes en conservant les zéros. Une forme compacte de rang r conserve les r occurrences de valeurs singulières strictement positives. Les noms varient : conserver les dimensions et le traitement des zéros fournis. Les applications rectangulaires et singulières sont admises ; aucune base propre ni aucun inverse n’est requis."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For A = diag(3,3,0) over the reals with the standard Euclidean inner product and an ordered orthonormal basis, U = V = I and Σ = A give an exact SVD. The two occurrences of singular value 3 give rank two, despite there being only one distinct positive value."
+msgstr "Pour A = diag(3,3,0) sur les réels avec le produit scalaire euclidien standard et une base orthonormée ordonnée, U = V = I et Σ = A donnent une SVD exacte. Les deux occurrences de la valeur singulière 3 donnent un rang de deux, bien qu’il n’existe qu’une seule valeur strictement positive distincte."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe supplied singular-value factors or results, retaining the linear map, scalar field, actual inner products, ordered coordinate bases and the precise dimensions and completeness of the declared form."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour décrire des facteurs ou résultats fournis de décomposition en valeurs singulières, en conservant l’application linéaire, le corps des scalaires, les produits scalaires effectifs, les bases de coordonnées ordonnées et les dimensions et la complétude précises de la forme déclarée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat a rank-truncated approximation as a complete exact factorization or identify a numerical tolerance-based rank with exact rank. Unordered singularValue links supply no multiplicity, ordering or left/right-vector association. Changing the inner products may change the singular values; the finite matrix statement does not cover arbitrary infinite-dimensional operators."
+msgstr "Ne pas traiter une approximation tronquée en rang comme une factorisation exacte complète ni identifier un rang numérique fondé sur une tolérance au rang exact. Des liens singularValue non ordonnés ne fournissent ni multiplicité, ni ordre, ni association aux vecteurs gauches et droits. Modifier les produits scalaires peut modifier les valeurs singulières ; l’énoncé matriciel fini ne couvre pas les opérateurs arbitraires en dimension infinie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Preserve supplied factor matrices, their shared ordering, multiplicities and exact or approximate status in the source representation. The registered skos:exactMatch to wd:Q420904 carries logic:SoundUnderApproximation preservation; a mapping, type or randomizedSVD descriptor does not certify an executed factorization."
+msgstr "Conserver les matrices de facteurs fournies, leur ordre commun, les multiplicités et le statut exact ou approché dans la représentation de la source. Le skos:exactMatch enregistré vers wd:Q420904 porte la préservation logic:SoundUnderApproximation ; une correspondance, un type ou un descripteur randomizedSVD ne certifie aucune factorisation exécutée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "singular value"
+msgstr "valeur singulière"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:SingularValueDecomposition to a math:Number representing one nonnegative real singular value σ, including zero when retained by the declared form. In orthonormal coordinates these values occupy the diagonal of Σ in A = UΣV*; the number is a resource rather than a bare literal."
+msgstr "Relie une math:SingularValueDecomposition à un math:Number représentant une valeur singulière réelle non négative σ, y compris zéro lorsque la forme déclarée le conserve. En coordonnées orthonormées, ces valeurs occupent la diagonale de Σ dans A = UΣV* ; le nombre est une ressource plutôt qu’un simple littéral."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For m×n A, its k = min(m,n) singular values are the nonnegative square roots of the largest k eigenvalues of A* A, counting multiplicity. When m < n, the other n-m eigenvalues of A* A are forced zeros. Singular values depend on the supplied inner products; they are not generally eigenvalues of A, their squares or explained-variance ratios."
+msgstr "Pour A de taille m×n, ses k = min(m,n) valeurs singulières sont les racines carrées non négatives des k plus grandes valeurs propres de A* A, comptées avec leur multiplicité. Lorsque m < n, les n-m autres valeurs propres de A* A sont nécessairement nulles. Les valeurs singulières dépendent des produits scalaires fournis ; elles ne sont pas en général les valeurs propres de A, leurs propres carrés ni des rapports de variance expliquée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real A = diag(3,3,0) with the standard Euclidean inner product, the singular-value sequence is 3, 3, 0 and exact rank is two. One unordered link to the number 3 cannot record both occurrences, and repeating the same RDF assertion does not add multiplicity."
+msgstr "Pour A = diag(3,3,0) réelle avec le produit scalaire euclidien standard, la suite des valeurs singulières est 3, 3, 0 et le rang exact est deux. Un lien non ordonné vers le nombre 3 ne peut pas consigner les deux occurrences, et répéter la même assertion RDF n’ajoute aucune multiplicité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied singular value as a number resource with its exact or approximate representation, decomposition context and source evidence for any occurrence multiplicity or factor position."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver une valeur singulière fournie comme ressource numérique avec sa représentation exacte ou approchée, le contexte de décomposition et les éléments de source établissant toute multiplicité d’occurrence ou position dans les facteurs."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not count distinct positive values or distinct RDF resources as exact rank. A truncated output set does not disclose omitted values, and absence of a zero output is not evidence of full rank. A numerical zero threshold is a supplied policy, never an implicit mathematical equality."
+msgstr "Ne pas compter les valeurs strictement positives distinctes ni les ressources RDF distinctes comme rang exact. Un ensemble de sorties tronqué ne révèle pas les valeurs omises, et l’absence de sortie nulle ne prouve pas le plein rang. Un seuil de zéro numérique est une politique fournie, jamais une égalité mathématique implicite."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied math:Number and preserve source ordering, occurrence multiplicities, factor associations and any numerical tolerance separately. This output relation supplies no left/right-vector pairing, default order, completeness witness or numerical computation."
+msgstr "Relier la décomposition au math:Number fourni et conserver séparément l’ordre de source, les multiplicités d’occurrence, les associations aux facteurs et toute tolérance numérique. Cette relation de sortie ne fournit ni appariement aux vecteurs gauches et droits, ni ordre par défaut, ni témoin de complétude, ni calcul numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Linear Map"
+msgstr "Application linéaire"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A total function T from a vector space V to a vector space W over the same scalar field, preserving linear combinations: T(av+bw) = aT(v)+bT(w). Its source and target vector-space structures are distinct in role from their carrier sets and from a matrix representing the map in chosen bases."
+msgstr "Une fonction totale T d’un espace vectoriel V vers un espace vectoriel W sur le même corps des scalaires, préservant les combinaisons linéaires : T(av+bw) = aT(v)+bT(w). Les structures vectorielles source et cible sont distinctes dans leur rôle de leurs ensembles supports et d’une matrice représentant l’application dans des bases choisies."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Linearity needs no inner product or finite-dimensional assumption. A finite matrix representation additionally needs ordered source and target bases. Changing coordinates for the same map over the same field preserves rank; a matrix label, frame or finite sample alone does not establish the universal linearity law."
+msgstr "La linéarité ne requiert ni produit scalaire ni hypothèse de dimension finie. Une représentation matricielle finie exige en plus des bases ordonnées à la source et à la cible. Changer les coordonnées d’une même application sur un même corps préserve le rang ; un libellé de matrice, un cadre ou un échantillon fini ne suffit pas à établir la loi universelle de linéarité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "Over the real numbers, T: R³ → R² given by T(x,y,z) = (x,y) is linear. In the standard ordered bases its matrix is [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]], its image is R², its rank is two and its kernel has dimension one."
+msgstr "Sur les réels, T: R³ → R² définie par T(x,y,z) = (x,y) est linéaire. Dans les bases ordonnées standard, sa matrice est [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]], son image est R², son rang est deux et son noyau a pour dimension un."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified linear map with declared source and target vector spaces over the same field, preserving their carriers, scalar actions and actual representation or defining rule."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour une application linéaire justifiée avec des espaces vectoriels source et cible déclarés sur le même corps, en conservant leurs supports, leurs actions scalaires et la représentation ou règle de définition effective."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer linearity from a matrix-shaped dataset or a neural-layer label. A nonzero bias translation is affine rather than linear, and a nonlinear activation does not become linear merely because its input has a weight matrix. Do not confuse a mathematical function with a functional RDF predicate or an executed method."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire la linéarité d’un jeu de données en forme de matrice ou d’un libellé de couche neuronale. Une translation par un biais non nul est affine plutôt que linéaire, et une activation non linéaire ne devient pas linéaire simplement parce que son entrée comporte une matrice de poids. Ne pas confondre une fonction mathématique avec un prédicat RDF fonctionnel ou une méthode exécutée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain the inherited math:Function frame through math:domain and math:codomain carrier-set resources; describe the vector-space structures and scalar field separately with existing vocabulary. Preserve any justified math:image. The registered skos:exactMatch to wd:Q207643 has logic:SoundUnderApproximation preservation; neither it nor the frame executes the map or proves linearity."
+msgstr "Conserver le cadre math:Function hérité au moyen de ressources d’ensembles supports liées par math:domain et math:codomain ; décrire séparément les structures vectorielles et le corps des scalaires avec le vocabulaire existant. Préserver toute math:image justifiée. Le skos:exactMatch enregistré vers wd:Q207643 a pour préservation logic:SoundUnderApproximation ; ni lui ni le cadre n’exécute l’application et ne prouve la linéarité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Rank"
+msgstr "Rang"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The dimension of the image of a math:LinearMap over its declared scalar field. A finite rank is a nonnegative integer, including zero, recorded through math:rankValue. The general image dimension may instead be infinite; the finite numeric property supplies no infinite-cardinal encoding."
+msgstr "La dimension de l’image d’une math:LinearMap sur son corps des scalaires déclaré. Un rang fini est un entier non négatif, y compris zéro, consigné par math:rankValue. La dimension générale de l’image peut au contraire être infinie ; la propriété numérique finie ne fournit aucun encodage de cardinal infini."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Rank concerns the attained image, not the declared source or target dimension. For a finite-dimensional source V, dim(V) = rank(T) + dim(kernel(T)); no finite-source conclusion is inferred for an arbitrary infinite-dimensional map. Rank also depends on the scalar-field interpretation of the vector spaces."
+msgstr "Le rang concerne l’image atteinte, pas la dimension déclarée de la source ou de la cible. Pour une source V de dimension finie, dim(V) = rang(T) + dim(noyau(T)) ; aucune conclusion propre à une source finie n’est déduite pour une application arbitraire en dimension infinie. Le rang dépend aussi de l’interprétation des espaces vectoriels sur leur corps des scalaires."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The real projection T: R³ → R², T(x,y,z) = (x,y), has rank two and nullity one. The zero map has rank zero, even when its source and target are nonzero vector spaces."
+msgstr "La projection réelle T: R³ → R², T(x,y,z) = (x,y), a pour rang deux et pour nullité un. L’application nulle a pour rang zéro, même lorsque sa source et sa cible sont des espaces vectoriels non nuls."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe the justified image dimension of an identified linear map in its actual field and vector-space context, keeping any finite numeric value separate from the map and its coordinate matrix."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour décrire la dimension justifiée de l’image d’une application linéaire identifiée dans son contexte effectif de corps et d’espaces vectoriels, en séparant toute valeur numérique finie de l’application et de sa matrice de coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute tensor-axis count, root-system rank, matrix size or a count of distinct output resources. In the finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product SVD setting, exact rank counts positive singular-value occurrences with multiplicity. Numerical tolerance and rank truncation are separate policies, not exact-rank proofs."
+msgstr "Ne pas substituer le nombre d’axes d’un tenseur, le rang d’un système de racines, la taille d’une matrice ou un nombre de ressources de sortie distinctes. Dans le cadre SVD préhilbertien réel ou complexe de dimension finie, le rang exact compte les occurrences de valeurs singulières strictement positives avec leur multiplicité. La tolérance numérique et la troncature en rang sont des politiques distinctes, pas des preuves du rang exact."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the rank as its own math:Rank resource and use math:rankValue for a justified finite value. Preserve the source identification of the relevant map and field in the existing representation; no dedicated rank-of property is supplied here. A type, number or grounding link alone does not calculate rank."
+msgstr "Décrire le rang comme sa propre ressource math:Rank et utiliser math:rankValue pour une valeur finie justifiée. Conserver l’identification de source de l’application concernée et du corps dans la représentation existante ; aucune propriété dédiée reliant le rang à son application n’est fournie ici. Un type, un nombre ou un lien de correspondance seul ne calcule pas le rang."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "rank value"
+msgstr "valeur du rang"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The nonnegative-integer value of a finite math:Rank: the dimension of the image of its associated linear map over the declared scalar field. Zero is an actual finite value. This datatype property records a supplied mathematical value; it does not compute or verify rank."
+msgstr "La valeur entière non négative d’un math:Rank fini : la dimension de l’image de son application linéaire associée sur le corps des scalaires déclaré. Zéro est une véritable valeur finie. Cette propriété de données consigne une valeur mathématique fournie ; elle ne calcule ni ne vérifie le rang."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The finite value contract has no fixed machine-width ceiling and no encoding for infinite-cardinal or unknown rank. The declared nonnegative-integer meaning is distinct from an executed lexical, range or cardinality check; no generated SHACL or native rank-validation result follows from this annotation."
+msgstr "Le contrat de valeur finie ne comporte aucun plafond de largeur machine fixe ni aucun encodage de rang cardinal infini ou inconnu. Le sens déclaré d’entier non négatif est distinct d’un contrôle lexical, de plage ou de cardinalité exécuté ; cette annotation n’implique aucun résultat de validation du rang par SHACL généré ou par le moteur natif."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real projection (x,y,z) ↦ (x,y), a supplied math:Rank resource can carry math:rankValue 2. The literal records the justified image dimension; the property does not infer the projection, its field or the argument establishing that value."
+msgstr "Pour la projection réelle (x,y,z) ↦ (x,y), une ressource math:Rank fournie peut porter math:rankValue 2. Le littéral consigne la dimension justifiée de l’image ; la propriété ne déduit ni la projection, ni son corps, ni l’argument établissant cette valeur."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when a finite image dimension is actually supplied and justified, preserving its integer literal and the source context that identifies the linear map and scalar field."
+msgstr "Utiliser lorsqu’une dimension finie de l’image est effectivement fournie et justifiée, en conservant son littéral entier et le contexte de source qui identifie l’application linéaire et le corps des scalaires."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace an unknown or infinite rank with zero, a large sentinel or an ambient dimension. Do not attach a rounded estimate or tolerance-based numerical rank as if it established the exact mathematical image dimension."
+msgstr "Ne pas remplacer un rang inconnu ou infini par zéro, une grande valeur sentinelle ou une dimension ambiante. Ne pas attacher une estimation arrondie ou un rang numérique fondé sur une tolérance comme s’il établissait la dimension mathématique exacte de l’image."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Attach the supplied nonnegative integer to the math:Rank resource and retain the map, field and supporting evidence in the existing source representation. Keep omission distinct from zero and preserve any separate approximation policy. The relation alone supplies no specialized validation gate or rank computation."
+msgstr "Attacher l’entier non négatif fourni à la ressource math:Rank et conserver l’application, le corps et les éléments justificatifs dans la représentation de source existante. Distinguer l’omission de zéro et préserver toute politique d’approximation distincte. La relation seule ne fournit aucun contrôle de validation spécialisé ni aucun calcul de rang."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Covariance Operator"
+msgstr "Opérateur de covariance"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A self-adjoint positive-semidefinite linear operator representing centered second moments in a declared real or complex inner-product setting. For finite-dimensional column coordinates with E[‖X‖²] finite, μ = E[X] and C = E[(X-μ)(X-μ)*], where * is conjugate transpose, or ordinary transpose over the reals."
+msgstr "Un opérateur linéaire autoadjoint positif semi-défini représentant les moments centrés d’ordre deux dans un cadre préhilbertien réel ou complexe déclaré. Pour des coordonnées colonnes de dimension finie avec E[‖X‖²] finie, μ = E[X] et C = E[(X-μ)(X-μ)*], où * est la transposée conjuguée, ou la transposée ordinaire sur les réels."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The coordinate formula uses supplied orthonormal bases and the complex convention ⟨u,v⟩ = u* v, conjugate-linear in the first argument. Infinite-dimensional use requires stated existence, boundedness and spectral hypotheses; this type does not assert a discrete eigenvector basis for an arbitrary operator. An unconjugated complex second moment is a different construction."
+msgstr "La formule en coordonnées utilise des bases orthonormées fournies et la convention complexe ⟨u,v⟩ = u* v, antilinéaire dans le premier argument. L’usage en dimension infinie exige des hypothèses déclarées d’existence, de bornitude et de spectre ; ce type n’affirme pas l’existence d’une base discrète de vecteurs propres pour un opérateur arbitraire. Un moment d’ordre deux complexe sans conjugaison est une autre construction."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A real random vector equally likely to be (1,0) or (-1,0) has mean zero and covariance diag(1,0) under the standard Euclidean inner product. This covariance is positive semidefinite and singular; its zero eigenvalue is valid, and no inverse is required."
+msgstr "Un vecteur aléatoire réel prenant (1,0) ou (-1,0) avec la même probabilité a une moyenne nulle et une covariance diag(1,0) pour le produit scalaire euclidien standard. Cette covariance est positive semi-définie et singulière ; sa valeur propre nulle est valide et aucun inverse n’est requis."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified population or empirical covariance operator, retaining the observations or probability model, scalar field, inner product, centering, scaling and actual normalization convention in the source representation."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour un opérateur de covariance de population ou empirique justifié, en conservant les observations ou le modèle probabiliste, le corps des scalaires, le produit scalaire, le centrage, la mise à l’échelle et la convention de normalisation effective dans la représentation de source."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer covariance from a Gram-matrix or symmetry label alone, require positive definiteness, or replace a missing operator with zero covariance. Repeated eigenvalues do not select unique eigenvectors. A declared covariance role or solver descriptor does not establish centering, covariance construction or numerical spectral analysis."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire une covariance d’un simple libellé de matrice de Gram ou de symétrie, exiger que l’opérateur soit défini positif ni remplacer un opérateur absent par une covariance nulle. Des valeurs propres répétées ne sélectionnent pas de vecteurs propres uniques. Un rôle de covariance déclaré ou un descripteur de solveur n’établit ni le centrage, ni la construction de covariance, ni une analyse spectrale numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain the inherited LinearMap and Function carrier-set frame separately from the vector-space structure. Use math:covarianceOperator from the analysis to this operator. Preserve sample orientation and divisor: empirical 1/N requires N > 0, while 1/(N-1) requires N > 1. Those choices and their evidence are supplied data, not defaults or new validation gates."
+msgstr "Conserver le cadre hérité d’ensembles supports de LinearMap et Function séparément de la structure vectorielle. Utiliser math:covarianceOperator de l’analyse vers cet opérateur. Préserver l’orientation des échantillons et le diviseur : la convention empirique 1/N exige N > 0, tandis que 1/(N-1) exige N > 1. Ces choix et leurs éléments justificatifs sont des données fournies, pas des valeurs par défaut ni de nouveaux contrôles de validation."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "covariance operator"
+msgstr "opérateur de covariance"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to the supplied math:CovarianceOperator that is its declared decomposition operand. The analysis process, its input data, the covariance operator and any reported numerical outputs retain separate roles; this link records the operator role rather than constructing it."
+msgstr "Relie une math:PCAAnalysis au math:CovarianceOperator fourni qui est son opérande déclaré de décomposition. Le processus d’analyse, ses données d’entrée, l’opérateur de covariance et toute sortie numérique rapportée conservent des rôles distincts ; ce lien consigne le rôle d’opérateur plutôt que de le construire."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The current PCA source contract requires at least one covariance-operator resource through its generic minimum and existing closure, associated with math:IncompletePCAAnalysis. This is not an exact-one or typed-target enforcement claim. The mathematical covariance meaning and the inherited operator frame still need their own evidence."
+msgstr "Le contrat source actuel de PCA exige au moins une ressource d’opérateur de covariance par son minimum générique et sa fermeture existante, associés à math:IncompletePCAAnalysis. Cela n’affirme pas un contrôle d’exactement une valeur ou de type de cible. Le sens mathématique de covariance et le cadre hérité de l’opérateur exigent encore leurs propres éléments justificatifs."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:residualPCA math:covarianceOperator p:residualCovariance and gives that CovarianceOperator domain and codomain p:covSpace. Its fixed Gram, dominant-axis and LDL calculations do not supply observed samples, an executed centering step or a sample-covariance normalization."
+msgstr "Le producteur exact-pca émet p:residualPCA math:covarianceOperator p:residualCovariance et donne à ce CovarianceOperator le domaine et le codomaine p:covSpace. Ses calculs sur un Gram fixe, d’axe dominant et de LDL ne fournissent ni échantillons observés, ni étape de centrage exécutée, ni normalisation de covariance d’échantillon."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain the actual covariance operand named by an analysis, together with independently supplied input, preprocessing, scalar-field, inner-product and normalization context."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver l’opérande effectif de covariance nommé par une analyse, avec les contextes d’entrée, de prétraitement, de corps des scalaires, de produit scalaire et de normalisation fournis indépendamment."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reverse the analysis-to-operator direction, substitute the dataset or solver for the operator, or infer an executed spectral decomposition from the edge. Missing covariance differs from a supplied operator, which may be zero or singular; no absent operand is repaired by inventing a zero operator or undeclared preprocessing."
+msgstr "Ne pas inverser la direction de l’analyse vers l’opérateur, substituer le jeu de données ou le solveur à l’opérateur ni déduire une décomposition spectrale exécutée de l’arête. Une covariance absente diffère d’un opérateur fourni, qui peut être nul ou singulier ; aucun opérande absent n’est réparé en inventant un opérateur nul ou un prétraitement non déclaré."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the analysis to its justified CovarianceOperator resource and preserve that operator’s carrier-set frame and actual construction evidence. Keep centering and scaling declarations on the analysis distinct from proof that those operations ran. The relation supplies no additional maximum, automatic target typing, covariance computation or numerical validation result."
+msgstr "Relier l’analyse à sa ressource CovarianceOperator justifiée et conserver le cadre d’ensembles supports de cet opérateur et les éléments de sa construction effective. Distinguer les déclarations de centrage et de mise à l’échelle sur l’analyse des preuves que ces opérations ont été exécutées. La relation ne fournit aucun maximum supplémentaire, typage automatique de cible, calcul de covariance ni résultat de validation numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Subspace"
+msgstr "Sous-espace vectoriel"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A vector subspace: a subset of a vector space closed under addition and scalar multiplication, itself a math:VectorSpace. A subclass of math:VectorSpace naming the space it sits in through math:subspaceOf. The image of a linear map is a subspace; an arbitrary embedding image or projection residual needs separate subspace justification. A math:OrthogonalComplement is the subspace orthogonal to an operand subspace within a declared inner-product space."
+msgstr "Un sous-espace vectoriel : une partie d’un espace vectoriel stable par addition et multiplication scalaire, elle-même un math:VectorSpace. Sous-classe de math:VectorSpace nommant l’espace qui la contient par math:subspaceOf. L’image d’une application linéaire est un sous-espace ; l’image d’un plongement arbitraire ou un résidu de projection exige une justification distincte de sa structure de sous-espace. Un math:OrthogonalComplement est le sous-espace orthogonal à un sous-espace opérande dans un espace à produit scalaire déclaré."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For W to be a subspace of V over F, W contains zero and uses the induced addition and scalar action of V, closed under every scalar in the same field F. Zero and whole-space subspaces, finite and infinite dimension are allowed. Algebraic closure here does not require topological closedness."
+msgstr "Pour que W soit un sous-espace de V sur F, W contient zéro et utilise l’addition et l’action scalaire induites de V, avec stabilité pour tout scalaire du même corps F. Le sous-espace nul, l’espace entier et les dimensions finies ou infinies sont admis. Cette stabilité algébrique n’exige pas que le sous-espace soit topologiquement fermé."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "In the real vector space R³ with its usual operations, W = {(x,y,0) : x,y in R} is a subspace, including zero and closed under real linear combinations. The affine plane {(x,y,1) : x,y in R} is not a subspace because it lacks zero."
+msgstr "Dans l’espace vectoriel réel R³ muni des opérations usuelles, W = {(x,y,0) : x,y dans R} est un sous-espace, contenant zéro et stable par combinaisons linéaires réelles. Le plan affine {(x,y,1) : x,y dans R} n’est pas un sous-espace, car il ne contient pas zéro."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified vector subspace with its ambient vector-space structure and common scalar field retained. A linear-map image or a supplied span can establish a subspace; sampled vectors alone do not establish closure of the sample set."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour un sous-espace vectoriel justifié, en conservant la structure de l’espace vectoriel ambiant et le corps des scalaires commun. L’image d’une application linéaire ou un espace engendré fourni peut établir un sous-espace ; des vecteurs échantillonnés seuls n’établissent pas la stabilité de l’ensemble des échantillons."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer a subspace from an embedding label, a dimension, an arbitrary nonlinear image or residual data. An orthogonal complement requires the declared ambient inner product; a global orthogonal direct-sum decomposition needs its own hypotheses in infinite dimension."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire un sous-espace d’un libellé de plongement, d’une dimension, d’une image non linéaire arbitraire ou de données résiduelles. Un complément orthogonal exige le produit scalaire ambiant déclaré ; une décomposition globale en somme directe orthogonale nécessite ses propres hypothèses en dimension infinie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe W as math:Subspace and link each justified ambient V with math:subspaceOf. Retain math:underlyingSet, math:structureOperation and math:satisfiesAxiom evidence separately from descriptive math:scalarField links. A type or ambient link supplies no automatic closure proof or subspace computation."
+msgstr "Décrire W comme math:Subspace et relier chaque espace ambiant V justifié par math:subspaceOf. Conserver les éléments justificatifs math:underlyingSet, math:structureOperation et math:satisfiesAxiom séparément des liens descriptifs math:scalarField. Un type ou un lien ambiant ne fournit ni preuve automatique de stabilité ni calcul de sous-espace."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "subspace of"
+msgstr "sous-espace de"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Subspace to the vector space it is a subspace of. Domain math:Subspace, range math:VectorSpace (stated in prose). The ambient space a subspace sits in, and against which its orthogonal complement is taken."
+msgstr "Relie un math:Subspace à l’espace vectoriel dont il est un sous-espace. Domaine math:Subspace, portée math:VectorSpace (indiqués en prose). L’espace ambiant qui contient le sous-espace et au sein duquel son complément orthogonal est pris."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is W to ambient V, with a common scalar field and induced operations justified separately. Several ambient links may be valid, including W to itself. The source states domain and range in prose without native typing, cardinality, inclusion, transitivity or closure rules for this property."
+msgstr "La direction va de W vers l’espace ambiant V, le corps des scalaires commun et les opérations induites étant justifiés séparément. Plusieurs liens ambiants peuvent être valides, y compris de W vers lui-même. La source énonce le domaine et la portée en prose, sans règles natives de typage, cardinalité, inclusion, transitivité ou stabilité pour cette propriété."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The linear-algebra-and-learning example states ex:embeddedSubspace math:subspaceOf ex:complexSpace4096. This records an asserted ambient relationship; the dataset supplies neither an embedding-image link to that subspace nor a proof of linear closure."
+msgstr "L’exemple linear-algebra-and-learning énonce ex:embeddedSubspace math:subspaceOf ex:complexSpace4096. Cela consigne une relation ambiante affirmée ; le jeu de données ne fournit ni lien entre l’image du plongement et ce sous-espace ni preuve de stabilité linéaire."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain each justified ambient vector space of a subspace without choosing a preferred ambient. Preserve the actual scalar-field interpretation and induced operations rather than infer them from shared dimensions or carrier labels."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver chaque espace vectoriel ambiant justifié d’un sous-espace sans choisir d’espace ambiant privilégié. Préserver l’interprétation effective du corps des scalaires et les opérations induites plutôt que les déduire de dimensions communes ou de libellés de supports."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reverse the relationship, substitute a carrier set or scalar field for the ambient vector-space structure, or treat the edge as a closure certificate. Keep math:orthogonalComplementOf for the operand subspace, math:ambientSpace for its enclosing space and math:definedByInnerProduct for its form; those role referents may coincide."
+msgstr "Ne pas inverser la relation, substituer un ensemble support ou un corps des scalaires à la structure vectorielle ambiante, ni traiter l’arête comme un certificat de stabilité. Conserver math:orthogonalComplementOf pour le sous-espace opérande, math:ambientSpace pour l’espace qui l’englobe et math:definedByInnerProduct pour sa forme ; les référents de ces rôles peuvent coïncider."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the supplied math:Subspace to its ambient math:VectorSpace and preserve the source justification of zero, addition and same-field scalar closure. For orthogonal-complement descriptions retain the separate operand, ambient and inner-product roles. Neither this edge nor a retrieved competency answer calculates a residual subspace."
+msgstr "Relier le math:Subspace fourni à son math:VectorSpace ambiant et conserver la justification de source pour zéro, l’addition et la stabilité scalaire sur le même corps. Pour décrire un complément orthogonal, conserver les rôles distincts d’opérande, d’espace ambiant et de produit scalaire. Ni cette arête ni une réponse de compétence extraite ne calcule un sous-espace résiduel."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Inner Product Space"
+msgstr "Espace préhilbertien"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A vector space equipped with an inner product — a math:VectorSpace carrying a math:innerProduct that assigns lengths and angles, so orthogonality and orthogonal complements are defined. A subclass of math:VectorSpace; the complex case carries a math:HermitianInnerProduct. It names the inner product it carries through math:innerProduct."
+msgstr "Un espace vectoriel muni d’un produit scalaire — un math:VectorSpace portant un math:innerProduct qui détermine longueurs et angles, de sorte que l’orthogonalité et les compléments orthogonaux sont définis. Sous-classe de math:VectorSpace ; le cas complexe porte un math:HermitianInnerProduct. Il nomme le produit scalaire dont il est muni par math:innerProduct."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The real case uses a symmetric positive-definite bilinear form; the complex case uses a conjugate-symmetric positive-definite sesquilinear form. Zero dimension, finite and infinite dimension are allowed. Completeness is an additional Hilbert-space condition, not a consequence of this type."
+msgstr "Le cas réel utilise une forme bilinéaire symétrique définie positive ; le cas complexe utilise une forme sesquilinéaire à symétrie hermitienne définie positive. La dimension nulle et les dimensions finies ou infinies sont admises. La complétude est une condition supplémentaire d’espace de Hilbert, pas une conséquence de ce type."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "On real R², h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 is an inner product with h(v,v) = v1² + 2 v2², positive for every nonzero v. The coordinate formula presupposes the supplied ordered basis and real scalar interpretation."
+msgstr "Sur R² réel, h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 est un produit scalaire avec h(v,v) = v1² + 2 v2², strictement positif pour tout v non nul. La formule en coordonnées suppose la base ordonnée fournie et l’interprétation réelle des scalaires."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when a vector space carries a justified inner product needed for lengths, norms or orthogonality. Retain the space, carrier set, scalar field, coordinate basis and form as separate roles."
+msgstr "Utiliser lorsqu’un espace vectoriel porte un produit scalaire justifié nécessaire aux longueurs, normes ou à l’orthogonalité. Conserver des rôles distincts pour l’espace, l’ensemble support, le corps des scalaires, la base de coordonnées et la forme."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer an inner product from a vector-space, norm or symmetric-matrix label alone, or treat positive-semidefinite or indefinite forms as positive-definite. An angle involving a zero vector is undefined, and complex angle conventions must be stated."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire un produit scalaire d’un simple libellé d’espace vectoriel, de norme ou de matrice symétrique, ni traiter une forme positive semi-définie ou indéfinie comme définie positive. Un angle impliquant un vecteur nul est indéfini, et les conventions d’angle complexe doivent être précisées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the vector-space structure and link its supplied form with math:innerProduct. Keep the inherited carrier, operation and law evidence explicit. A class or form link proves neither the inner-product laws nor completeness and does not invoke the finite real rational numeric core."
+msgstr "Décrire la structure vectorielle et relier sa forme fournie par math:innerProduct. Garder explicites le support, les opérations et les éléments justificatifs des lois hérités. Une classe ou un lien vers une forme ne prouve ni les lois du produit scalaire ni la complétude et n’invoque pas le noyau numérique rationnel réel de dimension finie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Hermitian Inner Product"
+msgstr "Produit scalaire hermitien"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A conjugate-symmetric, positive-definite sesquilinear form on a complex vector space — the inner product ⟨·,·⟩ of the complex case, linear in one argument and conjugate-linear in the other. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carried by a math:InnerProductSpace through math:innerProduct; it is the structure that defines a math:OrthogonalComplement in the complex (S⊥) case (math:definedByInnerProduct)."
+msgstr "Une forme sesquilinéaire à symétrie hermitienne définie positive sur un espace vectoriel complexe — le produit scalaire ⟨·,·⟩ du cas complexe, linéaire en un argument et antilinéaire en l’autre. Sous-classe de math:MathematicalObject portée par un math:InnerProductSpace via math:innerProduct ; c’est la structure qui définit un math:OrthogonalComplement dans le cas complexe (S⊥), par math:definedByInnerProduct."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Preserve which argument is conjugate-linear. Under the first-conjugate convention, h(au,bv) = conjugate(a) b h(u,v) and h(v,u) = conjugate(h(u,v)). Positive definiteness requires real h(v,v) > 0 for nonzero v, with h(0,0) = 0."
+msgstr "Préserver l’argument qui est antilinéaire. Selon la convention antilinéaire au premier argument, h(au,bv) = conjugate(a) b h(u,v) et h(v,u) = conjugate(h(u,v)). Le caractère défini positif exige h(v,v) réel et strictement positif pour v non nul, avec h(0,0) = 0."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "On C with h(z,w) = conjugate(z) w, h(i,1) = -i, h(1,i) = i and h(i,i) = 1. This form is conjugate-linear in the first argument and linear in the second; it is not complex bilinear."
+msgstr "Sur C avec h(z,w) = conjugate(z) w, h(i,1) = -i, h(1,i) = i et h(i,i) = 1. Cette forme est antilinéaire au premier argument et linéaire au second ; elle n’est pas bilinéaire sur les complexes."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified positive-definite Hermitian inner product on a complex vector space, retaining its actual scalar field, argument convention and coordinate representation independently."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour un produit scalaire hermitien défini positif justifié sur un espace vectoriel complexe, en conservant indépendamment son corps des scalaires effectif, sa convention d’arguments et sa représentation en coordonnées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not identify complex sesquilinearity with bilinearity or ordinary symmetry. A Hermitian matrix can be indefinite or positive semidefinite; its label or conjugate symmetry alone does not establish an inner product."
+msgstr "Ne pas identifier la sesquilinéarité complexe à la bilinéarité ou à la symétrie ordinaire. Une matrice hermitienne peut être indéfinie ou positive semi-définie ; son libellé ou sa seule symétrie hermitienne n’établit pas un produit scalaire."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the form as its own math:HermitianInnerProduct resource. Use math:innerProduct from its space and math:definedByInnerProduct from a complement where applicable. Retain evidence for the laws; these declarations do not execute a complex Hermitian calculation or construct a complement."
+msgstr "Nommer la forme comme sa propre ressource math:HermitianInnerProduct. Utiliser math:innerProduct depuis son espace et math:definedByInnerProduct depuis un complément le cas échéant. Conserver les éléments justificatifs des lois ; ces déclarations n’exécutent pas de calcul hermitien complexe et ne construisent pas de complément."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "inner product"
+msgstr "produit scalaire"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:InnerProductSpace to the inner product it carries — a math:HermitianInnerProduct in the complex case. Domain math:InnerProductSpace, range a math:HermitianInnerProduct or a real inner-product structure (stated in prose). The inner product is what makes orthogonality, and hence a math:OrthogonalComplement, well-defined."
+msgstr "Relie un math:InnerProductSpace au produit scalaire dont il est muni — un math:HermitianInnerProduct dans le cas complexe. Domaine math:InnerProductSpace, portée math:HermitianInnerProduct ou une structure de produit scalaire réel (indiqués en prose). Le produit scalaire rend bien définies l’orthogonalité et donc un math:OrthogonalComplement."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is space to form. The source states domain and range in prose without a native global functionality or typed-target rule for this property. Several supplied form descriptions do not select a preferred form or establish their equality."
+msgstr "La direction va de l’espace vers la forme. La source énonce le domaine et la portée en prose, sans règle native de fonctionnalité globale ou de typage de cible pour cette propriété. Plusieurs descriptions de formes fournies ne sélectionnent pas de forme privilégiée et n’établissent pas leur égalité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real u = (1,1) and v = (1,-1), the standard dot product is zero, while h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 is -1. Linking the intended form matters: the same vectors are orthogonal under one inner product and not the other."
+msgstr "Pour les vecteurs réels u = (1,1) et v = (1,-1), le produit scalaire usuel est nul, tandis que h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 vaut -1. Relier la forme voulue est essentiel : les mêmes vecteurs sont orthogonaux pour un produit scalaire et pas pour l’autre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to identify the actual inner product carried by a vector-space description, retaining the real or complex setting and the supplied form laws rather than inferring them from dimensions or labels."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour identifier le produit scalaire effectif porté par une description d’espace vectoriel, en conservant le cadre réel ou complexe et les lois de forme fournies plutôt que les déduire de dimensions ou de libellés."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute a scalar pairing result, coordinate matrix, basis or residual for the form. The edge neither transforms coordinates nor proves symmetry, sesquilinearity or positive definiteness."
+msgstr "Ne pas substituer un résultat scalaire d’appariement, une matrice de coordonnées, une base ou un résidu à la forme. L’arête ne transforme pas les coordonnées et ne prouve ni symétrie, ni sesquilinéarité, ni caractère défini positif."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Point math:innerProduct from the space to its supplied form resource. Preserve the carrier, scalar field, basis and argument convention separately. Retain each justified description without a preferred-form rule; a link does not invoke a numerical evaluator."
+msgstr "Diriger math:innerProduct de l’espace vers sa ressource de forme fournie. Préserver séparément le support, le corps des scalaires, la base et la convention d’arguments. Conserver chaque description justifiée sans règle de forme privilégiée ; un lien n’invoque pas d’évaluateur numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "defined by inner product"
+msgstr "défini par le produit scalaire"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:OrthogonalComplement to the inner product that defines orthogonality for it — the math:HermitianInnerProduct in the complex case. Domain math:OrthogonalComplement, range a math:HermitianInnerProduct or real inner-product structure (stated in prose). An orthogonal complement without a named inner product is ambiguous and ill-formed (math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement)."
+msgstr "Relie un math:OrthogonalComplement au produit scalaire qui définit son orthogonalité — le math:HermitianInnerProduct dans le cas complexe. Domaine math:OrthogonalComplement, portée math:HermitianInnerProduct ou une structure de produit scalaire réel (indiqués en prose). Un complément orthogonal sans produit scalaire nommé est ambigu et mal formé (math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement)."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The existing OrthogonalComplement-local source profile has minimum one, maximum one and all-values restrictions with logic:Thing, plus required-path closure and the associated math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement diagnostic. This generic resource contract does not prove that the target is a positive-definite Hermitian form."
+msgstr "Le profil source existant propre à OrthogonalComplement comporte des restrictions de minimum un, maximum un et de toutes les valeurs avec logic:Thing, ainsi qu’une fermeture de chemin requis et le diagnostic associé math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement. Ce contrat générique de ressource ne prouve pas que la cible est une forme hermitienne définie positive."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The ordinary linear-algebra-and-learning example states ex:residualSubspace math:definedByInnerProduct ex:hermitianInnerProduct, separately from its operand and ambient links. This names a defining form without evaluating it or proving the complement equation."
+msgstr "L’exemple ordinaire linear-algebra-and-learning énonce ex:residualSubspace math:definedByInnerProduct ex:hermitianInnerProduct, séparément de ses liens d’opérande et d’espace ambiant. Cela nomme une forme définissante sans l’évaluer ni prouver l’équation du complément."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when an orthogonal-complement description needs to retain the actual form defining orthogonality within its declared ambient space. Keep that form consistent with the supplied mathematical construction and argument convention."
+msgstr "Utiliser lorsqu’une description de complément orthogonal doit conserver la forme effective qui définit l’orthogonalité dans son espace ambiant déclaré. Garder cette forme cohérente avec la construction mathématique fournie et la convention d’arguments."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not confuse the complement-to-form direction with math:innerProduct from the ambient space. The class-local restriction is not global property functionality, automatic Hermitian target typing or proof that every complement vector is orthogonal to the operand."
+msgstr "Ne pas confondre la direction du complément vers la forme avec math:innerProduct depuis l’espace ambiant. La restriction locale à la classe n’est ni une fonctionnalité globale de propriété, ni un typage hermitien automatique de cible, ni une preuve que tout vecteur du complément est orthogonal à l’opérande."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the complement to its supplied form and retain math:orthogonalComplementOf, math:ambientSpace and math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement separately. Those roles need not have distinct referents. The competency query retrieves declarations; mathematical justification and computation remain separate evidence."
+msgstr "Relier le complément à sa forme fournie et conserver séparément math:orthogonalComplementOf, math:ambientSpace et math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement. Les référents de ces rôles ne sont pas nécessairement distincts. La requête de compétence extrait des déclarations ; justification mathématique et calcul restent des éléments justificatifs séparés."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Explained Variance"
+msgstr "Variance expliquée"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The share of positive finite total variance accounted for by a math:PrincipalComponent: its nonnegative covariance eigenvalue divided by the covariance trace, a dimensionless ratio in [0, 1]. A zero total variance leaves the ratio undefined. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:explainedVarianceRatio; the ratios across retained components quantify retained variance."
+msgstr "La part de la variance totale strictement positive et finie dont rend compte une math:PrincipalComponent : sa valeur propre de covariance non négative divisée par la trace de la covariance, un rapport sans dimension dans [0, 1]. Une variance totale nulle laisse le rapport indéfini. Sous-classe de math:MathematicalObject nommée par une PCA via math:explainedVarianceRatio ; les rapports des composantes retenues quantifient la variance conservée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This class records a normalized per-component share, distinct from an unnormalized variance amount. Finite covariance matrices use their trace as total variance. Infinite-dimensional use needs justified finite-trace spectral assumptions; no complete eigenbasis follows from this type."
+msgstr "Cette classe consigne une part normalisée par composante, distincte d’une quantité de variance non normalisée. Les matrices de covariance de dimension finie utilisent leur trace comme variance totale. L’usage en dimension infinie exige des hypothèses spectrales justifiées de trace finie ; ce type n’implique aucune base propre complète."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For covariance diag(3,1,0), total variance is 4 and the associated component ratios are 3/4, 1/4 and 0. Retaining only the first component retains 3/4 of total variance. Zero covariance instead gives an undefined ratio, not a ratio of zero."
+msgstr "Pour la covariance diag(3,1,0), la variance totale vaut 4 et les rapports des composantes associées valent 3/4, 1/4 et 0. Ne retenir que la première composante conserve 3/4 de la variance totale. Une covariance nulle donne au contraire un rapport indéfini, pas un rapport nul."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a supplied component share justified by its nonnegative covariance eigenvalue and positive finite total variance. Preserve the actual covariance, scalar field, basis, preprocessing and normalization evidence together with the source component association."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour une part de composante fournie, justifiée par sa valeur propre de covariance non négative et une variance totale strictement positive et finie. Préserver la covariance effective, le corps des scalaires, la base, les éléments justificatifs du prétraitement et de la normalisation, ainsi que l’association de source à la composante."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace missing data or zero-total undefined normalization with zero or one. A ratio sum of one can omit zero-variance components and does not prove a complete basis, semantic importance or predictive quality. Retained variance and cumulative shares are separate claims."
+msgstr "Ne pas remplacer des données manquantes ou une normalisation indéfinie due à un total nul par zéro ou un. Une somme de rapports égale à un peut omettre des composantes de variance nulle et ne prouve ni une base complète, ni une importance sémantique, ni une qualité prédictive. La variance conservée et les parts cumulées sont des affirmations distinctes."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the result as math:ExplainedVariance and link it from the analysis with math:explainedVarianceRatio. Preserve its supplied magnitude, component association, order and multiplicity in the existing source representation. A descriptor alone supplies no numeric value or normalization computation."
+msgstr "Nommer le résultat math:ExplainedVariance et le relier depuis l’analyse par math:explainedVarianceRatio. Préserver sa grandeur fournie, son association à la composante, son ordre et sa multiplicité dans la représentation de source existante. Un descripteur seul ne fournit ni valeur numérique ni calcul de normalisation."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "explained variance ratio"
+msgstr "rapport de variance expliquée"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:ExplainedVariance it produces — the share of total variance a component accounts for. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:ExplainedVariance (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "Relie une math:PCAAnalysis à une math:ExplainedVariance qu’elle produit — la part de variance totale dont rend compte une composante. Domaine math:PCAAnalysis, portée math:ExplainedVariance (indiqués en prose). Une sortie déclarée de l’analyse."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The property signature is stated in prose. The existing PCA-local profile has a generic logic:Thing minimum and all-values restriction plus required-path closure, without a dedicated maximum, typed-target rule or numeric denominator/range proof."
+msgstr "La signature de la propriété est énoncée en prose. Le profil existant propre à PCA comporte un minimum générique et une restriction de toutes les valeurs avec logic:Thing, ainsi qu’une fermeture de chemin requis, sans maximum dédié, règle de typage de cible ou preuve numérique du dénominateur ou de l’intervalle."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:residualPCA math:explainedVarianceRatio p:pc1Variance and types that descriptor as math:ExplainedVariance. Its fixed Gram, dominant-axis and LDL results supply neither a numeric ratio nor a PCA eigenvalue family."
+msgstr "Le producteur exact-pca émet p:residualPCA math:explainedVarianceRatio p:pc1Variance et type ce descripteur math:ExplainedVariance. Ses résultats sur un Gram fixe, d’axe dominant et de LDL ne fournissent ni rapport numérique ni famille de valeurs propres de PCA."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a justified normalized component-result resource declared by a PCA analysis. Keep the source evidence identifying its actual component, covariance and normalization context independently of the other output relations."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver une ressource de résultat normalisé de composante justifiée, déclarée par une analyse PCA. Garder les éléments de source identifiant sa composante effective, sa covariance et son contexte de normalisation indépendamment des autres relations de sortie."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute a literal, eigenvalue amount or singular value for this result resource. Unordered component and variance links do not establish pairings. The current competency query joins those roles independently; its rows are not numeric association certificates."
+msgstr "Ne pas substituer un littéral, une valeur propre non normalisée ou une valeur singulière à cette ressource de résultat. Des liens non ordonnés de composante et de variance n’établissent pas d’appariements. La requête de compétence actuelle joint ces rôles indépendamment ; ses lignes ne certifient pas les associations numériques."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Point the property from the analysis to the supplied math:ExplainedVariance resource. Preserve its actual source value and component association without inferring order, repeated occurrences or a default ratio. The link alone performs no normalization or numeric validation."
+msgstr "Diriger la propriété de l’analyse vers la ressource math:ExplainedVariance fournie. Préserver sa valeur de source effective et son association à la composante sans déduire d’ordre, d’occurrences répétées ou de rapport par défaut. Le lien seul n’effectue ni normalisation ni validation numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Principal Component"
+msgstr "Composante principale"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A principal component: one orthonormal direction of maximal remaining variance produced by a math:PCAAnalysis — an eigenvector of the math:CovarianceOperator. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, named by an analysis through math:principalComponent, carrying a math:LoadingVector (its coefficients) and explaining a share of variance (math:ExplainedVariance). Its MEANING is never an intrinsic property: what a component encodes is a math:ResidualInterpretationClaim held from a vantage."
+msgstr "Une composante principale : une direction d’un ensemble orthonormé, de variance restante maximale, produite par une math:PCAAnalysis — un vecteur propre du math:CovarianceOperator. Sous-classe de math:MathematicalObject, nommée par une analyse via math:principalComponent, portant un math:LoadingVector (ses coefficients) et expliquant une part de variance (math:ExplainedVariance). Sa SIGNIFICATION n’est jamais une propriété intrinsèque : ce qu’une composante encode est une math:ResidualInterpretationClaim tenue depuis un point de vue."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "GMEOW uses the direction convention: a normalized nonzero covariance eigenvector in a declared geometry. The PCA review also uses component for a linear combination of variables. Keep that score-variable usage distinct from this direction and its LoadingVector coefficient representation; these roles impose no class disjointness or resource inequality."
+msgstr "GMEOW adopte la convention de direction : un vecteur propre de covariance normalisé et non nul dans une géométrie déclarée. La revue sur la PCA emploie aussi composante pour une combinaison linéaire de variables. Distinguer cet usage de variable de scores de cette direction et de sa représentation en coefficients LoadingVector ; ces rôles n’imposent ni disjonction de classes ni inégalité de ressources."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real covariance diag(3,1,0) in the standard Euclidean basis, the coordinate directions have eigenvalues 3, 1 and 0. The third unit direction is still a valid component direction; its zero eigenvalue does not make the vector zero."
+msgstr "Pour la covariance réelle diag(3,1,0) dans la base euclidienne standard, les directions coordonnées ont pour valeurs propres 3, 1 et 0. La troisième direction unitaire reste une direction de composante valide ; sa valeur propre nulle ne rend pas le vecteur nul."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified PCA output direction, retaining the covariance, scalar field, inner product, preprocessing, normalization and selected component family in the source evidence."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour une direction de sortie PCA justifiée, en conservant dans les éléments de source la covariance, le corps des scalaires, le produit scalaire, le prétraitement, la normalisation et la famille de composantes sélectionnée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer semantic importance, computed scores or a unique preferred direction from this type. Repeated eigenvalues permit different eigenspace bases, sign or complex phase choices persist, and a truncated family need not span the input. Zero dimension supplies no nonzero component."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire de ce type une importance sémantique, des scores calculés ou une direction préférée unique. Les valeurs propres répétées permettent différentes bases d’espace propre, les choix de signe ou de phase complexe subsistent, et une famille tronquée ne couvre pas nécessairement l’espace d’entrée. La dimension zéro ne fournit aucune composante non nulle."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the analysis through math:principalComponent and retain ordered component and coefficient associations in the source representation. Keep any interpretation in a vantage-bearing math:ResidualInterpretationClaim; an output descriptor alone proves neither orthonormality nor an executed eigendecomposition."
+msgstr "Relier l’analyse via math:principalComponent et conserver les associations ordonnées entre composantes et coefficients dans la représentation de source. Garder toute interprétation dans une math:ResidualInterpretationClaim portée par un point de vue ; un descripteur de sortie seul ne prouve ni l’orthonormalité ni l’exécution d’une décomposition propre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "principal component"
+msgstr "composante principale"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to one of the math:PrincipalComponent directions it produces. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:PrincipalComponent (stated in prose). The declared component outputs; a PCA producing none is ill-formed (math:IncompletePCAAnalysis)."
+msgstr "Relie une math:PCAAnalysis à l’une des directions math:PrincipalComponent qu’elle produit. Domaine math:PCAAnalysis, portée math:PrincipalComponent (indiqués en prose). Les sorties de composantes déclarées ; une PCA n’en produisant aucune est mal formée (math:IncompletePCAAnalysis)."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This analysis-to-direction relation has a prose-only signature. The PCA-local generic Thing minimum, all-values restriction and required-path closure supply no dedicated maximum, automatic PrincipalComponent target typing, numerical normalization or variance ordering."
+msgstr "Cette relation de l’analyse vers la direction possède une signature énoncée uniquement en prose. Le minimum générique sur Thing, la restriction de toutes les valeurs et la fermeture de chemin requis propres à PCA ne fournissent ni maximum dédié, ni typage automatique des cibles PrincipalComponent, ni normalisation numérique, ni ordre de variance."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "An analysis can declare two supplied directions through math:principalComponent. The two unordered links retain those output roles without saying which has greater variance or which loading and score resources belong to either direction."
+msgstr "Une analyse peut déclarer deux directions fournies via math:principalComponent. Ces deux liens non ordonnés conservent les rôles de sortie sans indiquer laquelle a la plus grande variance ni quelles ressources de coefficients et de scores appartiennent à chaque direction."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to record the principal directions that a supplied PCA reports, preserving their identities and the actual field, covariance and component-selection evidence."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour consigner les directions principales rapportées par une PCA fournie, en préservant leurs identités ainsi que les éléments effectifs concernant le corps, la covariance et la sélection des composantes."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat resource counts, IRI names or repeated RDF assertions as component rank, multiplicity, ordering or a complete basis. Missing directions are not zero directions; never invent a component merely to fill the required role."
+msgstr "Ne pas traiter les nombres de ressources, les noms d’IRI ou les assertions RDF répétées comme un rang de composante, une multiplicité, un ordre ou une base complète. Des directions manquantes ne sont pas des directions nulles ; ne jamais inventer une composante pour remplir le rôle requis."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Keep math:loadingVector, math:scoreVector and math:explainedVarianceRatio as separate analysis-output roles, with their actual associations retained in the source. The current competency query joins components and variance descriptors independently; its IRI ordering establishes no numeric pairing."
+msgstr "Garder math:loadingVector, math:scoreVector et math:explainedVarianceRatio comme des rôles de sortie d’analyse séparés, avec leurs associations effectives conservées dans la source. La requête de compétence actuelle joint indépendamment les composantes et les descripteurs de variance ; son ordre d’IRI n’établit aucun appariement numérique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Loading Vector"
+msgstr "Vecteur de coefficients"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A loading vector: the coefficients of a math:PrincipalComponent in the original coordinates — how each input feature contributes to the component. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:loadingVector. Loadings are the eigenvectors of the math:CovarianceOperator; their INTERPRETATION is a math:ResidualInterpretationClaim, not an intrinsic property."
+msgstr "Un vecteur de coefficients : les coefficients d’une math:PrincipalComponent dans les coordonnées d’origine — la contribution de chaque caractéristique d’entrée à la composante. Sous-classe de math:MathematicalObject nommée par une PCA via math:loadingVector. Ces vecteurs de coefficients sont les vecteurs propres du math:CovarianceOperator ; leur INTERPRÉTATION est une math:ResidualInterpretationClaim, pas une propriété intrinsèque."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This is the coefficient-vector convention: the coordinates of a component direction in a supplied ordered feature basis for the prepared input. Retain the normalization convention; a coordinate representation is distinct from the geometric direction without requiring different RDF resources."
+msgstr "Il s’agit de la convention de vecteur de coefficients : les coordonnées d’une direction de composante dans une base ordonnée de caractéristiques fournie pour l’entrée préparée. Conserver la convention de normalisation ; une représentation en coordonnées est distincte de la direction géométrique sans exiger des ressources RDF différentes."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "In the standard real basis, a component with loading coefficients (1,0,0) selects the first prepared feature. The zero entries are valid coefficients of a nonzero unit vector; they are not missing data or zero-variance conclusions."
+msgstr "Dans la base réelle standard, une composante de coefficients (1,0,0) sélectionne la première caractéristique préparée. Les entrées nulles sont des coefficients valides d’un vecteur unitaire non nul ; ce ne sont ni des données manquantes ni des conclusions de variance nulle."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for supplied component coefficients with feature identities, basis order, field, units, centering/scaling and normalization evidence. Coefficients in standardized features are not automatically coefficients in unprocessed physical units."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour des coefficients de composante fournis, avec les identités des caractéristiques, l’ordre de base, le corps, les unités et les éléments justificatifs du centrage, de la mise à l’échelle et de la normalisation. Des coefficients de caractéristiques standardisées ne sont pas automatiquement des coefficients dans les unités physiques non traitées."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not silently substitute correlation-scaled loadings, biplot markers, factor-analysis loadings or importance scores. Correlation needs nonzero feature and component-score variances; a zero eigenvalue leaves the corresponding correlation undefined, not zero. A zero feature scale licenses no division."
+msgstr "Ne pas substituer silencieusement des coefficients redimensionnés en corrélations, des marqueurs de biplot, des coefficients d’analyse factorielle ou des scores d’importance. Une corrélation exige des variances non nulles de la caractéristique et des scores de composante ; une valeur propre nulle laisse la corrélation correspondante indéfinie, pas nulle. Une échelle de caractéristique nulle n’autorise aucune division."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the supplied result from its analysis with math:loadingVector and retain component/feature associations and any coordinate transformation in the source representation. Changes of sign, phase or tied-eigenspace basis require consistent score coordinates; interpretation remains a vantage-bearing claim."
+msgstr "Nommer le résultat fourni depuis son analyse avec math:loadingVector et conserver les associations composante/caractéristique et toute transformation de coordonnées dans la représentation de source. Les changements de signe, de phase ou de base dans un espace propre de valeur répétée exigent des coordonnées de scores cohérentes ; l’interprétation reste une affirmation portée par un point de vue."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "loading vector"
+msgstr "vecteur de coefficients"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:LoadingVector it produces — the coefficients of a component in the original features. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:LoadingVector (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "Relie une math:PCAAnalysis à un math:LoadingVector qu’elle produit — les coefficients d’une composante dans les caractéristiques d’origine. Domaine math:PCAAnalysis, portée math:LoadingVector (indiqués en prose). Une sortie déclarée de l’analyse."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is analysis to coefficient resource. Its signature is stated in prose; the generic PCA-local Thing minimum, all-values restriction and closure establish no typed target, dedicated maximum, coordinate length or component-to-loading pairing."
+msgstr "La direction va de l’analyse à la ressource de coefficients. Sa signature est énoncée en prose ; le minimum générique sur Thing, la restriction de toutes les valeurs et la fermeture propres à PCA n’établissent ni cible typée, ni maximum dédié, ni longueur de coordonnées, ni appariement composante-vecteur de coefficients."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact Gram/PCA producer links its analysis to pc1Loadings and types that descriptor math:LoadingVector. It supplies no numeric loading coefficients, so the declaration is not evidence that a covariance eigenvector was computed."
+msgstr "Le producteur exact Gram/PCA relie son analyse à pc1Loadings et type ce descripteur math:LoadingVector. Il ne fournit aucun coefficient numérique ; cette déclaration ne prouve donc pas qu’un vecteur propre de covariance a été calculé."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain identified loading outputs of the stated analysis, alongside the source's component, feature-order, preprocessing and coefficient-normalization context."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour conserver les sorties de coefficients identifiées de l’analyse indiquée, avec le contexte de source des composantes, de l’ordre des caractéristiques, du prétraitement et de la normalisation des coefficients."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer one loading per component, an ordered association or a numeric payload from link counts or matching resource names. This relation does not compute coefficients or convert correlation-scaled loadings into the selected coefficient convention."
+msgstr "Ne pas déduire un vecteur de coefficients par composante, une association ordonnée ou une charge utile numérique du nombre de liens ou de noms de ressources concordants. Cette relation ne calcule pas les coefficients et ne convertit pas les coefficients redimensionnés en corrélations dans la convention de coefficients sélectionnée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe a justified LoadingVector result and preserve its supplied coordinates and associations through the existing source representation. Retain the actual input transformation and its scale conditions; neither a link nor a policy label performs centering, scaling or spectral analysis."
+msgstr "Décrire un résultat LoadingVector justifié et préserver ses coordonnées et associations fournies dans la représentation de source existante. Conserver la transformation effective de l’entrée et ses conditions d’échelle ; ni un lien ni une étiquette de politique n’effectuent le centrage, la mise à l’échelle ou l’analyse spectrale."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Score Vector"
+msgstr "Vecteur de scores"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A score vector: the coordinates of a data point projected onto the principal components — the representation of a sample in the PCA basis. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:scoreVector. Scores are inputs projected through the loadings."
+msgstr "Un vecteur de scores : les coordonnées d’un point de données projeté sur les composantes principales — la représentation d’une observation dans la base PCA. Sous-classe de math:MathematicalObject nommée par une PCA via math:scoreVector. Les scores sont les entrées projetées au moyen des coefficients."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "GMEOW uses one sample's tuple across retained components. A component's scores across samples are a different view of the score matrix. Preserve sample identity and component order; neither this role nor the loading/direction roles imply global class disjointness."
+msgstr "GMEOW utilise le tuple d’une observation sur les composantes retenues. Les scores d’une composante sur les observations sont une vue différente de la matrice des scores. Préserver l’identité de l’observation et l’ordre des composantes ; ni ce rôle ni ceux de coefficients/direction n’impliquent une disjonction globale de classes."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For prepared real sample (2,-1,4) and ordered loading columns (1,0,0) and (0,1,0), the sample score tuple is (2,-1). It retains two projection coordinates, not the omitted third coordinate or a complete reconstruction."
+msgstr "Pour l’observation réelle préparée (2,-1,4) et les colonnes ordonnées de coefficients (1,0,0) et (0,1,0), le tuple de scores de l’observation est (2,-1). Il conserve deux coordonnées de projection, pas la troisième coordonnée omise ni une reconstruction complète."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for supplied coordinates of an identified sample in a declared retained PCA frame, keeping its input transformation, field, geometry, component order and projection evidence."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour les coordonnées fournies d’une observation identifiée dans un repère PCA retenu déclaré, en conservant la transformation de l’entrée, le corps, la géométrie, l’ordre des composantes et les éléments justificatifs de la projection."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not read scores as nonnegative variance ratios, loading coefficients or semantic importance. Zero tuples and negative entries can be valid. A zero score tuple is not an invalid zero eigenvector, and a truncated tuple need not recover the input."
+msgstr "Ne pas lire les scores comme des rapports de variance non négatifs, des coefficients de composante ou une importance sémantique. Les tuples nuls et les entrées négatives peuvent être valides. Un tuple de scores nul n’est pas un vecteur propre nul invalide, et un tuple tronqué ne permet pas nécessairement de retrouver l’entrée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "In a finite real Euclidean convention with prepared observation rows X and ordered loading columns A, T = X A has sample tuples in rows and one component's scores in each column. Retain those associations in the source; complex or other geometries need their actual conjugation and inner-product conventions."
+msgstr "Dans une convention euclidienne réelle de dimension finie, avec les observations préparées en lignes de X et les coefficients ordonnés en colonnes de A, T = X A contient les tuples d’observation en lignes et les scores d’une composante dans chaque colonne. Conserver ces associations dans la source ; les géométries complexes ou autres exigent leurs conventions effectives de conjugaison et de produit scalaire."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "score vector"
+msgstr "vecteur de scores"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:ScoreVector it produces — a data point's coordinates in the principal-component basis. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:ScoreVector (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "Relie une math:PCAAnalysis à un math:ScoreVector qu’elle produit — les coordonnées d’un point de données dans la base de composantes principales. Domaine math:PCAAnalysis, portée math:ScoreVector (indiqués en prose). Une sortie déclarée de l’analyse."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This links an analysis to a supplied sample-coordinate resource, not a numeric literal. Its prose-only signature and PCA-local generic Thing minimum, all-values restriction and closure establish no typed target, dedicated maximum, sample association or tuple-dimension proof."
+msgstr "Cette propriété relie une analyse à une ressource fournie de coordonnées d’observation, pas à un littéral numérique. Sa signature uniquement en prose et le minimum générique sur Thing, la restriction de toutes les valeurs et la fermeture propres à PCA n’établissent ni cible typée, ni maximum dédié, ni association à une observation, ni preuve de dimension du tuple."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The ordinary scene names sampleScores through math:scoreVector and types it math:ScoreVector. It gives no numeric tuple or sample-association structure; the resource name alone does not supply either."
+msgstr "La scène ordinaire nomme sampleScores via math:scoreVector et le type math:ScoreVector. Elle ne donne ni tuple numérique ni structure d’association à une observation ; le nom de la ressource ne fournit à lui seul ni l’un ni l’autre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to catalogue supplied sample-score outputs of the declared analysis, retaining each sample identity, component-position correspondence and preprocessing/projection context in the source evidence."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour cataloguer les sorties de scores d’observation fournies de l’analyse déclarée, en conservant dans les éléments de source chaque identité d’observation, la correspondance des positions de composantes et le contexte de prétraitement/projection."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace absent scores with zero tuples or infer that all samples were projected. This output link and the producer's Gram/LDL calculations do not compute sample scores or establish feature/component pairing."
+msgstr "Ne pas remplacer des scores absents par des tuples nuls ni déduire que toutes les observations ont été projetées. Ce lien de sortie et les calculs Gram/LDL du producteur ne calculent pas les scores d’observation et n’établissent pas d’appariement caractéristique/composante."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Keep the result linked from its analysis and retain its actual sample, ordered components, coefficient representation and prepared input together in the source. The current competency query retrieves component and variance roles without retrieving or validating score coordinates."
+msgstr "Garder le résultat relié depuis son analyse et conserver ensemble dans la source son observation effective, les composantes ordonnées, la représentation en coefficients et l’entrée préparée. La requête de compétence actuelle extrait les rôles de composante et de variance sans extraire ni valider les coordonnées de scores."
diff --git slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
index e640c2633..10c8c847d 100644
--- slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
+++ slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
@@ -2826,13 +2826,13 @@ msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/metricSignature|skos:definition"
 msgid "Relates a math:MetricTensor, math:QuadraticSpace, math:QuadraticForm, or math:CliffordAlgebra to its shared math:MetricSignature (p, q). Range math:MetricSignature (stated in prose). Structured, not an opaque string, so metric and Clifford consumers read the same exact sign convention."
 msgstr "将 math:MetricTensor、math:QuadraticSpace、math:QuadraticForm 或 math:CliffordAlgebra 关联到其共享的 math:MetricSignature (p, q)。值域为 math:MetricSignature（以文字说明）。它是结构化对象而非不透明字符串，因此度量和 Clifford 使用方读取完全相同的符号约定。"
 
-msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|rdfs:label"
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
 msgid "has basis"
 msgstr "具有基"
 
-msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|skos:definition"
-msgid "Relates a math:VectorSpace, math:QuadraticSpace, or math:CliffordAlgebra to a math:Basis of its carrier. Range math:Basis (stated in prose). A space or algebra may carry several bases; a Clifford basis fixes the ordered generators used by its exact products and blade witnesses."
-msgstr "将向量空间、二次空间或 Clifford 代数关联到其载体的 math:Basis；Clifford 基确定精确乘积所用的有序生成元。"
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:VectorSpace, math:QuadraticSpace or math:CliffordAlgebra to a math:Basis of its vector-space carrier. The relation names a basis choice and permits several choices; it does not enumerate or order basis elements. A Clifford algebra carrier basis is distinct from its ordered grade-one generators."
+msgstr "将 math:VectorSpace、math:QuadraticSpace 或 math:CliffordAlgebra 关联到其向量空间载体的 math:Basis。该关系命名一个基的选择，并允许多个选择；它不枚举基元素，也不规定其顺序。Clifford 代数载体的基与其有序一级生成元不同。"
 
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/analysisInput|rdfs:label"
 msgid "analysis input"
@@ -3266,8 +3266,8 @@ msgid "Bilinear Form"
 msgstr "双线性型"
 
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
-msgid "A bilinear form B on a vector space: a map B(·, ·) that is linear in each argument separately. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Its definiteness (math:definiteness) records whether it is positive-definite, positive-semidefinite, indefinite, or negative-definite; represented in a math:Basis it becomes a math:Matrix. An inner product is a positive-definite symmetric (or Hermitian) bilinear form; the symmetric case is math:SymmetricBilinearForm."
-msgstr "向量空间上的双线性型 B：映射 B(·, ·) 对每个参数分别线性。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类。其定号性（math:definiteness）记录正定、半正定、不定或负定；在某个 math:Basis 中表示时得到 math:Matrix。内积是正定的对称（或埃尔米特）双线性型；对称情形为 math:SymmetricBilinearForm。"
+msgid "A bilinear form B on a vector space: a map B(·, ·) that is linear in each argument separately. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject. Its definiteness (math:definiteness) records whether it is positive-definite, positive-semidefinite, indefinite, or negative-definite; represented in a math:Basis it becomes a math:Matrix. A real inner product is a positive-definite symmetric bilinear form; a complex inner product is a positive-definite Hermitian sesquilinear form. The symmetric bilinear case is math:SymmetricBilinearForm."
+msgstr "向量空间上的双线性型 B：映射 B(·, ·) 对每个参数分别线性。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类。其定号性（math:definiteness）记录正定、半正定、不定或负定；在某个 math:Basis 中表示时得到 math:Matrix。实内积是正定对称双线性型；复内积是正定厄米半双线性型。对称双线性情形为 math:SymmetricBilinearForm。"
 
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/BilinearForm|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
 msgid "Use for a scalar-valued pairing that is linear in each of its two vector arguments, independently of the coordinates chosen to represent it."
@@ -17478,3 +17478,803 @@ msgstr "策略有助于规定目标问题。在提供分析方法及其缺失数
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/missingnessMechanism|skos:scopeNote"
 msgid "Declares a missingness assumption, distinct from math:hasMissingnessIndicator recording absence, math:missingDataPolicy describing supplied analysis handling, and an event-specific target strategy named through math:intercurrentEventHandling. An assumption is not itself a handling procedure."
 msgstr "声明缺失机制假设，区别于记录缺失的 math:hasMissingnessIndicator、描述已提供分析处理方式的 math:missingDataPolicy，以及通过 math:intercurrentEventHandling 命名的事件专属目标策略。假设本身不是处理程序。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RatioQuantity|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Ratio quantity"
+msgstr "比值量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/RatioQuantity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A quantity interpreted in a quotient reference frame with explicit numerator and denominator frames. Its magnitude uses math:quantityValue and its dimension uses math:hasDimension; frame composition preserves the two unit contexts rather than making every dimensionless ratio interchangeable. This quantity form is distinct from the integer representation of math:RationalValue."
+msgstr "在商参考系中解释的量，明确保留分子与分母参考系。其量值使用 math:quantityValue，量纲使用 math:hasDimension；参考系组合保留两个单位语境，并不使所有无量纲比值都可互换。这种量形式不同于 math:RationalValue 的整数表示。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuotientReferenceFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Quotient reference frame"
+msgstr "商参考系"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/QuotientReferenceFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A reference frame whose unit interpretation is one explicitly identified numerator frame per one explicitly identified denominator frame. It retains the ordinary reference-frame profile and both component identities. This structural composition supplies no implicit scale factor, currency conversion, frame equivalence or general quotient evaluator."
+msgstr "其单位解释为一个明确标识的分子参考系除以一个明确标识的分母参考系的参考系。它保留普通参考系描述及两个组成参考系的身份。这种结构组合不提供隐含比例因子、货币兑换、参考系等价关系或通用商求值器。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numeratorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "numerator frame"
+msgstr "分子参考系"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/numeratorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The numerator reference frame of a math:QuotientReferenceFrame. For a selected unit-price quantity this is the currency frame, not a monetary amount or a numeric numerator."
+msgstr "math:QuotientReferenceFrame 的分子参考系。对于选定的单价量，它是货币参考系，而不是货币金额或数值分子。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/denominatorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "denominator frame"
+msgstr "分母参考系"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/denominatorFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The denominator reference frame of a math:QuotientReferenceFrame. For a selected unit-price quantity this identifies the counted-unit frame; equality of physical dimensions alone does not identify that frame."
+msgstr "math:QuotientReferenceFrame 的分母参考系。对于选定的单价量，它标识所计单位的参考系；仅有物理量纲相等并不能确定该参考系。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteRatioFrame|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Incomplete ratio frame"
+msgstr "不完整的比值参考系"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/IncompleteRatioFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A conformance failure in which a RatioQuantity lacks its unique quotient reference frame or a QuotientReferenceFrame lacks a unique, correctly typed numerator or denominator frame. It identifies missing or conflicting structure, not a failed numerical division."
+msgstr "RatioQuantity 缺少唯一商参考系，或 QuotientReferenceFrame 缺少唯一且类型正确的分子或分母参考系时发生的符合性失败。它标识缺失或冲突的结构，而不是数值除法失败。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecRatioQuantityFramed|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "A dimensioned RatioQuantity declares one QuotientReferenceFrame with one typed numerator and denominator frame. Its complete component contexts remain distinct and no arithmetic result is asserted."
+msgstr "带有维度的 RatioQuantity 声明一个 QuotientReferenceFrame，其中分子和分母各有一个已定型的参考系。完整的分量上下文保持彼此独立，且不声明任何算术结果。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecRatioQuantityMissingFrame|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The framed control with only the RatioQuantity hasReferenceFrame edge removed must raise IncompleteRatioFrame from the canonical closed required path. Its dimension and the unused complete quotient remain valid."
+msgstr "仅移除了 RatioQuantity 的 hasReferenceFrame 边的参考系对照必须由规范的封闭必需路径报告 IncompleteRatioFrame。其维度和未使用的完整商参考系仍然有效。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecQuotientFrameMissingDenominator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The framed control with only denominatorFrame removed must raise IncompleteRatioFrame from the quotient's closed required denominator path. The numerator, quantity frame and ordinary reference profiles remain supplied."
+msgstr "仅移除了 denominatorFrame 的参考系对照必须由商参考系的封闭必需分母路径报告 IncompleteRatioFrame。分子、数量参考系及普通参考系配置仍然齐全。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Basis"
+msgstr "基"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "An algebraic basis of a vector space over its scalar field: a linearly independent spanning family. Every vector has unique finitely supported coefficients indexed by the basis elements. The basis is distinct from an ordering of its elements, a coordinate array and an inner product."
+msgstr "向量空间在其标量域上的代数基，即线性无关且张成该空间的族。每个向量都具有以基元素为索引的唯一有限支撑系数。基与其元素的排序、坐标数组及内积彼此不同。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Uniqueness is relative to the vector space and scalar field. Indexed coefficients need not form an ordered tuple; positional coordinates additionally require a correspondence between positions and basis elements. A named Basis record alone does not establish independence or spanning."
+msgstr "唯一性相对于向量空间及标量域而言。带索引的系数不一定构成有序元组；位置坐标还需要位置与基元素之间的对应关系。仅命名一个 Basis 记录不能证明线性无关性或张成性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer declares p:covBasis as math:Basis and links its Gram matrix to that resource through math:inBasis. The RDF names the context but does not enumerate basis elements or their order."
+msgstr "exact-pca 生成器将 p:covBasis 声明为 math:Basis，并通过 math:inBasis 将其 Gram 矩阵关联到该资源。RDF 命名了上下文，但没有枚举基元素或其顺序。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to name a supplied basis underlying vectors, coordinate arrays or an algebra carrier, retaining the actual vector space and scalar field."
+msgstr "用于命名向量、坐标数组或代数载体所依据的已提供基，同时保留实际的向量空间及标量域。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer orthonormality or eigenvector roles from the Basis type. A self-adjoint operator on a finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product space admits an orthonormal eigenbasis; not every basis is an eigenbasis. Do not extend that conclusion to arbitrary infinite-dimensional self-adjoint operators or assume that truncated PCA components span the full input space."
+msgstr "不要从 Basis 类型推断标准正交性或特征向量角色。有限维实或复内积空间上的自伴算子具有标准正交特征向量基，但并非每个基都是特征向量基。不要将该结论推广到任意无限维自伴算子，也不要假定截断的主成分张成整个输入空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Basis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the basis as its own resource. Use math:hasBasis on the supplied space or algebra and math:inBasis on a vector or Gram matrix. Preserve any supplied element inventory and ordering evidence; neither link constructs a basis or computes a coordinate transform."
+msgstr "将基描述为独立资源。在已提供的空间或代数上使用 math:hasBasis，在向量或 Gram 矩阵上使用 math:inBasis。保留任何已提供的元素清单及顺序证据；这两个链接都不会构造基或计算坐标变换。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "In the finite real Cl(p,q) profile, the algebra carrier has dimension 2^(p+q), while there are p+q grade-one generators. The producer emits selected generator records through math:hasBasisBlade; those records do not enumerate the complete carrier basis or prove independence and spanning."
+msgstr "在有限实 Cl(p,q) 配置中，代数载体的维数为 2^(p+q)，而一级生成元有 p+q 个。生成器通过 math:hasBasisBlade 输出选定的生成元记录；这些记录既未枚举载体的完整基，也不证明线性无关性或张成性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The Clifford producer names a separate BladeBasis through math:hasBasis and emits grade-one math:BasisBlade records with math:generatorIndex. The named carrier basis and the indexed generator records retain different roles."
+msgstr "Clifford 生成器通过 math:hasBasis 命名独立的 BladeBasis，并输出带有 math:generatorIndex 的一级 math:BasisBlade 记录。已命名的载体基与带索引的生成元记录保持不同角色。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to record an actual basis choice for a vector space, quadratic space or algebra carrier, including several supplied choices without selecting a preferred basis."
+msgstr "用于记录向量空间、二次空间或代数载体的实际基选择，包括保留多个已提供的选择而不选出首选基。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not count the emitted grade-one generator records as the full algebra carrier basis or treat generator order as a complete blade-basis order. A hasBasis link alone does not prove linear independence or spanning and does not choose an unrecorded default."
+msgstr "不要将输出的一级生成元记录计为代数载体的完整基，也不要将生成元顺序视为完整基刃的排序。单独的 hasBasis 链接不能证明线性无关性或张成性，也不会选取未记录的默认基。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the supplied space or algebra to its Basis resource with math:hasBasis. Retain the CliffordAlgebra class-local requirement for a typed basis without making this property globally functional. Record supplied generator indices separately and use math:inBasis for coordinate representations."
+msgstr "通过 math:hasBasis 将已提供的空间或代数关联到其 Basis 资源。保留 CliffordAlgebra 类局部要求的已定型基，而不将该属性设为全局函数属性。单独记录已提供的生成元索引，并使用 math:inBasis 描述坐标表示。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "in basis"
+msgstr "在基下"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:GramMatrix or math:Vector to the math:Basis relative to which its entries or coordinates are recorded. The link identifies the declared basis context; it does not supply the element inventory, its order or a coordinate transformation."
+msgstr "将 math:GramMatrix 或 math:Vector 关联到记录其元素或坐标时所依据的 math:Basis。该链接标识已声明的基上下文，但不提供元素清单、元素顺序或坐标变换。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Matrix row/column indices and vector component indices are positions. Interpreting them as basis elements additionally requires the supplied position-to-element correspondence. The exact producer names p:covBasis only as Basis, so its inBasis edge alone does not publish such an ordered inventory."
+msgstr "矩阵行列索引与向量分量索引表示位置。要将其解释为基元素，还需要已提供的位置与元素对应关系。精确生成器仅将 p:covBasis 命名为 Basis，因此单独的 inBasis 边不会发布这样的有序清单。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:pcaGram math:inBasis p:covBasis and separately p:pcaGram math:representsForm p:covForm. These identify the coordinate context and represented form, without enumerating the basis elements or their order."
+msgstr "exact-pca 生成器输出 p:pcaGram math:inBasis p:covBasis，并单独输出 p:pcaGram math:representsForm p:covForm。这些链接标识坐标上下文与所表示的形式，但不枚举基元素或其顺序。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to preserve the actual basis context of supplied Gram-matrix entries or vector coordinates, separately from the coordinate-independent vector or bilinear form."
+msgstr "用于保留已提供的 Gram 矩阵元素或向量坐标的实际基上下文，并与不依赖坐标的向量或双线性形式分开描述。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat a basis label or inBasis link as proof that an indexed array is complete, correctly ordered or expressed in that basis. Changing the link alone does not transform the entries, and no conversion between differently based arrays is implicit."
+msgstr "不要将基的标签或 inBasis 链接视为索引数组完整、排序正确或在该基下表示的证明。仅修改链接不会变换数组元素，不同基下的数组之间也不隐含任何转换。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/inBasis|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Attach math:inBasis to the supplied vector or Gram matrix and retain any explicit basis-element ordering with its indexed components or entries. Keep math:representsForm separate from the coordinate context. A basis change needs an actual transformation and its inputs; this relation records no such execution."
+msgstr "在已提供的向量或 Gram 矩阵上附加 math:inBasis，并将任何显式基元素顺序与带索引的分量或元素一同保留。将 math:representsForm 与坐标上下文分开。基变换需要实际的变换及其输入；此关系不记录这样的执行。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Eigendecomposition"
+msgstr "特征分解"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A decomposition of a linear operator into eigenvalue and nonzero eigenvector data. In finite dimension, the diagonalization A = QΛQ⁻¹ requires a complete eigenbasis: Q is invertible, its columns are eigenvectors, and the diagonal entries of Λ are their eigenvalues in matching order."
+msgstr "将线性算子分解为特征值和非零特征向量数据的分解。在有限维情形下，对角化 A = QΛQ⁻¹ 要求完整的特征向量基：Q 可逆，其列为特征向量，Λ 的对角元素是按相同顺序对应的特征值。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The operator acts on the declared vector space over its scalar field; any extension of scalars is explicit. Not every operator is diagonalizable. Orthonormal or unitary eigenbasis claims require additional inner-product and operator hypotheses; the finite-dimensional formula does not assert an eigenvector basis for arbitrary infinite-dimensional operators."
+msgstr "算子作用于已声明标量域上的已声明向量空间；任何标量扩张都应显式给出。并非每个算子都可对角化。声称标准正交特征向量基或酉特征向量矩阵需要额外的内积和算子假设；有限维公式并不声称任意无限维算子都存在特征向量基。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For A = diag(0,3) over the real numbers in a supplied ordered basis, Q = I and Λ = diag(0,3) give a complete diagonalization. Q is invertible although A is singular; the zero eigenvalue has the nonzero eigenvector (1,0)."
+msgstr "对于实数域上在已提供有序基下的 A = diag(0,3)，Q = I 和 Λ = diag(0,3) 给出完整对角化。虽然 A 是奇异矩阵，Q 仍可逆；零特征值具有非零特征向量 (1,0)。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe supplied eigenvalue and eigenvector data for an operator, retaining the operator, vector space, scalar field and evidence for any claimed complete diagonalization."
+msgstr "用于描述已提供的算子特征值和特征向量数据，保留算子、向量空间、标量域以及任何完整对角化声明的依据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer pairing, order, multiplicity or completeness from separate unordered math:eigenvalue and math:eigenvector links. Equal output counts, distinct node identities or repeated RDF assertions do not establish these facts, and the two output sets do not imply a Cartesian product of valid eigenpairs."
+msgstr "不要从分开且无序的 math:eigenvalue 和 math:eigenvector 链接推断配对、顺序、重数或完整性。输出数量相等、节点标识不同或重复的 RDF 断言均不能证明这些事实；两个输出集合也不意味着其笛卡尔积中的所有配对都是有效特征对。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Eigendecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain actual source associations and ordering in their supplied representation. The registered skos:closeMatch to wd:Q190524 has logic:ValidationOnly preservation; it neither supplies an OpenMath eigen correspondence nor certifies numerical execution. A type or eigensolver descriptor alone proves no result."
+msgstr "在来源所提供的表示中保留实际的关联和顺序。已登记的、指向 wd:Q190524 的 skos:closeMatch 采用 logic:ValidationOnly 保持判定；它既不提供 OpenMath 特征对应关系，也不认证数值执行。仅有类型或特征求解器描述符不能证明任何结果。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "eigenvalue"
+msgstr "特征值"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Eigendecomposition to a math:Number representing a scalar λ for which Av = λv holds for some nonzero vector v in the declared vector space. The scalar belongs to the declared field, which may be real or complex; the number is a resource rather than a bare literal."
+msgstr "将 math:Eigendecomposition 关联到表示标量 λ 的 math:Number，且已声明向量空间中存在非零向量 v 使 Av = λv 成立。标量属于已声明的域，该域可以是实数域或复数域；该数以资源而非裸字面量表示。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Zero is a valid eigenvalue. In finite dimension, algebraic multiplicity counts a root of the characteristic polynomial, while geometric multiplicity is the dimension of its eigenspace. Neither is a count of distinct RDF number resources, and repeated identical RDF edges do not record multiplicity."
+msgstr "零是有效特征值。在有限维情形下，代数重数是特征多项式根的重数，几何重数则是对应特征子空间的维数。两者都不是不同 RDF 数值资源的数量，重复相同的 RDF 边也不记录重数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real matrix A = diag(0,3), λ = 0 is an eigenvalue associated with v = (1,0). A math:eigenvalue link to the number resource records the scalar output; its association with this vector still needs the supplied source evidence."
+msgstr "对于实矩阵 A = diag(0,3)，λ = 0 是与 v = (1,0) 关联的特征值。指向数值资源的 math:eigenvalue 链接记录标量输出；它与此向量的关联仍需来源所提供的依据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied eigenvalue as a number resource with its exact or approximate representation and the operator and scalar-field context of the decomposition."
+msgstr "用于将已提供的特征值保留为数值资源，并保留其精确或近似表示，以及分解的算子和标量域上下文。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reject λ = 0, assume every real operator has real eigenvalues, or silently extend the scalar field. Do not pair this output with every math:eigenvector output or infer pairings from equal counts or RDF order."
+msgstr "不要排除 λ = 0，不要假定每个实算子都具有实特征值，也不要静默扩张标量域。不要将此输出与每个 math:eigenvector 输出配对，也不要从数量相等或 RDF 顺序推断配对。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvalue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied math:Number. Preserve its numeric representation and any source association, ordering and multiplicity evidence separately; this property alone supplies none of them and performs no eigensolver computation."
+msgstr "将分解关联到已提供的 math:Number。单独保留其数值表示以及任何来源提供的关联、顺序和重数依据；该属性本身不提供这些信息，也不执行特征求解计算。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "eigenvector"
+msgstr "特征向量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Eigendecomposition to a nonzero vector v satisfying Av = λv for an associated scalar λ, relative to the declared operator, vector space and scalar field. The vector is a mathematical object; its coordinates additionally depend on the supplied basis."
+msgstr "将 math:Eigendecomposition 关联到非零向量 v；相对于已声明的算子、向量空间和标量域，该向量与关联标量 λ 满足 Av = λv。向量是数学对象；其坐标还依赖于已提供的基。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "A nonzero scalar multiple remains an eigenvector for the same eigenvalue. Normalization and choice of representatives are additional data. Several independent vectors may share an eigenvalue, and a list of output resources alone establishes neither their independence nor the dimension of that eigenspace."
+msgstr "非零标量倍数仍是同一特征值的特征向量。归一化和代表元选择属于额外数据。多个线性无关向量可以共享一个特征值，仅有输出资源列表既不能证明其线性无关性，也不能确定该特征子空间的维数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real matrix A = diag(0,3), v = (1,0) is a nonzero eigenvector with λ = 0, and 2v is another representative of the same eigendirection. The zero vector satisfies the equation but is not an eigenvector."
+msgstr "对于实矩阵 A = diag(0,3)，v = (1,0) 是对应 λ = 0 的非零特征向量，2v 则是同一特征方向的另一个代表元。零向量满足方程，但不是特征向量。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied nonzero eigenvector output with its vector-space and scalar-field context, preserving any coordinate basis and actual source association to its eigenvalue."
+msgstr "用于保留已提供的非零特征向量输出及其向量空间和标量域上下文，并保留任何坐标基以及来源提供的与其特征值的实际关联。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat the zero vector as an eigenvector or infer unit norm, orthogonality, a complete eigenbasis or an eigenvalue pairing from this link. A selected or truncated component family need not span the input space."
+msgstr "不要将零向量视为特征向量，也不要从此链接推断单位范数、正交性、完整特征向量基或与某个特征值的配对。选定或截断的分量族不一定张成输入空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/eigenvector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied vector resource and retain its coordinates, basis, normalization and association evidence as provided. Keep eigenvalue associations explicit in the source representation; separate unordered output links neither construct eigenpairs nor execute a solver."
+msgstr "将分解关联到已提供的向量资源，并按来源保留其坐标、基、归一化及关联依据。在来源表示中显式保留特征值关联；分开且无序的输出链接既不构造特征对，也不执行求解器。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Singular Value Decomposition"
+msgstr "奇异值分解"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A factorization of a linear map between finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product spaces. In orthonormal coordinates A = UΣV*, with orthonormal factor columns appropriate to the declared form, nonnegative real diagonal entries in Σ and V* the conjugate transpose (ordinary transpose over the reals)."
+msgstr "有限维实或复内积空间之间线性映射的分解。在标准正交坐标下，A = UΣV*，其中因子矩阵的列按所声明形式满足标准正交条件，Σ 的对角元素为非负实数，V* 表示共轭转置（实数情形下为普通转置）。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For m×n A, a full form has U m×m, Σ m×n and V n×n; a thin form may use k = min(m,n) columns, retaining zeros. A compact rank-r form retains the r positive singular-value occurrences. Names vary: retain supplied dimensions and zero treatment. Rectangular and singular maps are admitted; no eigenbasis or inverse is required."
+msgstr "对于 m×n 的 A，完整形式中 U 为 m×m、Σ 为 m×n、V 为 n×n；薄形式可以使用 k = min(m,n) 列并保留零值。秩为 r 的紧致形式保留 r 个正奇异值出现项。命名惯例各异，应保留来源提供的维数及零值处理方式。矩形映射和奇异映射均可采用此分解，无需特征向量基或逆。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For A = diag(3,3,0) over the reals with the standard Euclidean inner product and an ordered orthonormal basis, U = V = I and Σ = A give an exact SVD. The two occurrences of singular value 3 give rank two, despite there being only one distinct positive value."
+msgstr "对于实数域上采用标准欧氏内积及有序标准正交基的 A = diag(3,3,0)，U = V = I 和 Σ = A 给出精确 SVD。奇异值 3 出现两次，因此秩为二，尽管不同的正值只有一个。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe supplied singular-value factors or results, retaining the linear map, scalar field, actual inner products, ordered coordinate bases and the precise dimensions and completeness of the declared form."
+msgstr "用于描述已提供的奇异值分解因子或结果，保留线性映射、标量域、实际内积、有序坐标基以及所声明形式的确切维数和完整性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat a rank-truncated approximation as a complete exact factorization or identify a numerical tolerance-based rank with exact rank. Unordered singularValue links supply no multiplicity, ordering or left/right-vector association. Changing the inner products may change the singular values; the finite matrix statement does not cover arbitrary infinite-dimensional operators."
+msgstr "不要将截断秩近似视为完整精确分解，也不要将基于数值容差的秩等同于精确秩。无序的 singularValue 链接不提供重数、顺序或与左右奇异向量的关联。改变内积可能改变奇异值；有限矩阵结论不适用于任意无限维算子。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/SingularValueDecomposition|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Preserve supplied factor matrices, their shared ordering, multiplicities and exact or approximate status in the source representation. The registered skos:exactMatch to wd:Q420904 carries logic:SoundUnderApproximation preservation; a mapping, type or randomizedSVD descriptor does not certify an executed factorization."
+msgstr "在来源表示中保留已提供的因子矩阵、共同顺序、重数及精确或近似状态。已登记的、指向 wd:Q420904 的 skos:exactMatch 采用 logic:SoundUnderApproximation 保持判定；对应关系、类型或 randomizedSVD 描述符均不能认证已执行的分解。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "singular value"
+msgstr "奇异值"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:SingularValueDecomposition to a math:Number representing one nonnegative real singular value σ, including zero when retained by the declared form. In orthonormal coordinates these values occupy the diagonal of Σ in A = UΣV*; the number is a resource rather than a bare literal."
+msgstr "将 math:SingularValueDecomposition 关联到表示一个非负实奇异值 σ 的 math:Number；若声明的形式保留零值，则包括零。在标准正交坐标下，这些值位于 A = UΣV* 中 Σ 的对角线上；该数以资源而非裸字面量表示。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For m×n A, its k = min(m,n) singular values are the nonnegative square roots of the largest k eigenvalues of A* A, counting multiplicity. When m < n, the other n-m eigenvalues of A* A are forced zeros. Singular values depend on the supplied inner products; they are not generally eigenvalues of A, their squares or explained-variance ratios."
+msgstr "对于 m×n 的 A，其 k = min(m,n) 个奇异值是 A* A 按重数计算的最大 k 个特征值的非负平方根。当 m < n 时，A* A 的其余 n-m 个特征值必为零。奇异值依赖于已提供的内积；一般而言，它们不同于 A 的特征值、自身的平方或解释方差比。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real A = diag(3,3,0) with the standard Euclidean inner product, the singular-value sequence is 3, 3, 0 and exact rank is two. One unordered link to the number 3 cannot record both occurrences, and repeating the same RDF assertion does not add multiplicity."
+msgstr "对于采用标准欧氏内积的实矩阵 A = diag(3,3,0)，奇异值序列为 3、3、0，精确秩为二。指向数值 3 的一个无序链接不能记录两次出现，重复同一 RDF 断言也不会增加重数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a supplied singular value as a number resource with its exact or approximate representation, decomposition context and source evidence for any occurrence multiplicity or factor position."
+msgstr "用于将已提供的奇异值保留为数值资源，并保留其精确或近似表示、分解上下文以及来源提供的任何出现重数或因子位置依据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not count distinct positive values or distinct RDF resources as exact rank. A truncated output set does not disclose omitted values, and absence of a zero output is not evidence of full rank. A numerical zero threshold is a supplied policy, never an implicit mathematical equality."
+msgstr "不要将不同的正值数量或不同 RDF 资源数量作为精确秩。截断的输出集合不披露被省略的值，未输出零值也不构成满秩依据。数值零阈值是已提供的策略，绝不意味着隐含的数学相等。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/singularValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the decomposition to the supplied math:Number and preserve source ordering, occurrence multiplicities, factor associations and any numerical tolerance separately. This output relation supplies no left/right-vector pairing, default order, completeness witness or numerical computation."
+msgstr "将分解关联到已提供的 math:Number，并单独保留来源顺序、出现重数、因子关联及任何数值容差。该输出关系不提供左右奇异向量配对、默认顺序、完整性见证或数值计算。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Linear Map"
+msgstr "线性映射"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A total function T from a vector space V to a vector space W over the same scalar field, preserving linear combinations: T(av+bw) = aT(v)+bT(w). Its source and target vector-space structures are distinct in role from their carrier sets and from a matrix representing the map in chosen bases."
+msgstr "从同一标量域上的向量空间 V 到向量空间 W 的全函数 T，保持线性组合：T(av+bw) = aT(v)+bT(w)。源和目标的向量空间结构在角色上不同于各自的载体集合，也不同于在选定基下表示该映射的矩阵。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Linearity needs no inner product or finite-dimensional assumption. A finite matrix representation additionally needs ordered source and target bases. Changing coordinates for the same map over the same field preserves rank; a matrix label, frame or finite sample alone does not establish the universal linearity law."
+msgstr "线性性不需要内积或有限维假设。有限矩阵表示还需要有序的源基和目标基。对同一域上的同一映射改变坐标会保持秩；仅有矩阵标签、框架或有限样本不能证明普遍的线性规律。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "Over the real numbers, T: R³ → R² given by T(x,y,z) = (x,y) is linear. In the standard ordered bases its matrix is [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]], its image is R², its rank is two and its kernel has dimension one."
+msgstr "在实数域上，T: R³ → R²，T(x,y,z) = (x,y)，是线性映射。在标准有序基下，其矩阵为 [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]]，像为 R²，秩为二，核的维数为一。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified linear map with declared source and target vector spaces over the same field, preserving their carriers, scalar actions and actual representation or defining rule."
+msgstr "用于有依据的线性映射，其源和目标向量空间应声明在同一域上，并保留它们的载体、标量作用及实际表示或定义规则。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer linearity from a matrix-shaped dataset or a neural-layer label. A nonzero bias translation is affine rather than linear, and a nonlinear activation does not become linear merely because its input has a weight matrix. Do not confuse a mathematical function with a functional RDF predicate or an executed method."
+msgstr "不要从矩阵形状的数据集或神经网络层标签推断线性性。非零偏置平移是仿射而非线性的，非线性激活也不会仅因其输入具有权重矩阵而变为线性。不要将数学函数与函数型 RDF 谓词或已执行的方法混淆。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LinearMap|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain the inherited math:Function frame through math:domain and math:codomain carrier-set resources; describe the vector-space structures and scalar field separately with existing vocabulary. Preserve any justified math:image. The registered skos:exactMatch to wd:Q207643 has logic:SoundUnderApproximation preservation; neither it nor the frame executes the map or proves linearity."
+msgstr "通过 math:domain 和 math:codomain 指向载体集合资源，保留继承的 math:Function 框架；使用现有词汇单独描述向量空间结构及标量域。保留任何有依据的 math:image。已登记的、指向 wd:Q207643 的 skos:exactMatch 采用 logic:SoundUnderApproximation 保持判定；该对应关系及框架均不执行映射，也不证明线性性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Rank"
+msgstr "秩"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The dimension of the image of a math:LinearMap over its declared scalar field. A finite rank is a nonnegative integer, including zero, recorded through math:rankValue. The general image dimension may instead be infinite; the finite numeric property supplies no infinite-cardinal encoding."
+msgstr "math:LinearMap 的像在其已声明标量域上的维数。有限秩是非负整数，包括零，通过 math:rankValue 记录。一般的像维数也可能是无限的；有限数值属性不提供无限基数编码。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Rank concerns the attained image, not the declared source or target dimension. For a finite-dimensional source V, dim(V) = rank(T) + dim(kernel(T)); no finite-source conclusion is inferred for an arbitrary infinite-dimensional map. Rank also depends on the scalar-field interpretation of the vector spaces."
+msgstr "秩描述实际达到的像，而非已声明的源或目标维数。对于有限维源空间 V，dim(V) = rank(T) + dim(kernel(T))；不能对任意无限维映射推断仅适用于有限维源的结论。秩还依赖于向量空间的标量域解释。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The real projection T: R³ → R², T(x,y,z) = (x,y), has rank two and nullity one. The zero map has rank zero, even when its source and target are nonzero vector spaces."
+msgstr "实投影 T: R³ → R²，T(x,y,z) = (x,y)，秩为二，零度为一。零映射的秩为零，即使其源和目标都是非零向量空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to describe the justified image dimension of an identified linear map in its actual field and vector-space context, keeping any finite numeric value separate from the map and its coordinate matrix."
+msgstr "用于在已标识线性映射的实际域和向量空间上下文中描述有依据的像维数，并将任何有限数值与映射及其坐标矩阵分开保留。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute tensor-axis count, root-system rank, matrix size or a count of distinct output resources. In the finite-dimensional real or complex inner-product SVD setting, exact rank counts positive singular-value occurrences with multiplicity. Numerical tolerance and rank truncation are separate policies, not exact-rank proofs."
+msgstr "不要用张量轴数、根系的秩、矩阵大小或不同输出资源的数量代替秩。在有限维实或复内积空间的 SVD 情形下，精确秩按重数计算正奇异值的出现项。数值容差和秩截断属于独立策略，不构成精确秩证明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Rank|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the rank as its own math:Rank resource and use math:rankValue for a justified finite value. Preserve the source identification of the relevant map and field in the existing representation; no dedicated rank-of property is supplied here. A type, number or grounding link alone does not calculate rank."
+msgstr "将秩描述为独立的 math:Rank 资源，并用 math:rankValue 记录有依据的有限值。在现有表示中保留来源对相关映射及标量域的标识；此处不提供专用的秩所属映射属性。仅有类型、数值或对应关系链接不会计算秩。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "rank value"
+msgstr "秩值"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The nonnegative-integer value of a finite math:Rank: the dimension of the image of its associated linear map over the declared scalar field. Zero is an actual finite value. This datatype property records a supplied mathematical value; it does not compute or verify rank."
+msgstr "有限 math:Rank 的非负整数值，即其关联线性映射的像在已声明标量域上的维数。零是实际的有限值。该数据类型属性记录已提供的数学值，不计算或验证秩。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The finite value contract has no fixed machine-width ceiling and no encoding for infinite-cardinal or unknown rank. The declared nonnegative-integer meaning is distinct from an executed lexical, range or cardinality check; no generated SHACL or native rank-validation result follows from this annotation."
+msgstr "有限值契约不设固定机器位宽上限，也不编码无限基数秩或未知秩。已声明的非负整数含义与已执行的词法、范围或基数检查不同；不能从此注释推断已生成 SHACL 或原生秩验证的结果。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For the real projection (x,y,z) ↦ (x,y), a supplied math:Rank resource can carry math:rankValue 2. The literal records the justified image dimension; the property does not infer the projection, its field or the argument establishing that value."
+msgstr "对于实投影 (x,y,z) ↦ (x,y)，已提供的 math:Rank 资源可以携带 math:rankValue 2。该字面量记录有依据的像维数；属性不会推断投影、标量域或确立该值的论证。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when a finite image dimension is actually supplied and justified, preserving its integer literal and the source context that identifies the linear map and scalar field."
+msgstr "用于实际提供且有依据的有限像维数，保留整数字面量以及标识线性映射和标量域的来源上下文。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace an unknown or infinite rank with zero, a large sentinel or an ambient dimension. Do not attach a rounded estimate or tolerance-based numerical rank as if it established the exact mathematical image dimension."
+msgstr "不要用零、大的哨兵值或环境维数代替未知秩或无限秩。不要将四舍五入估计或基于容差的数值秩附加为已确立精确数学像维数的值。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/rankValue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Attach the supplied nonnegative integer to the math:Rank resource and retain the map, field and supporting evidence in the existing source representation. Keep omission distinct from zero and preserve any separate approximation policy. The relation alone supplies no specialized validation gate or rank computation."
+msgstr "将已提供的非负整数附加到 math:Rank 资源，并在现有来源表示中保留映射、标量域及支持依据。将省略与零分开，并保留任何独立的近似策略。该关系本身不提供专门的验证关卡或秩计算。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Covariance Operator"
+msgstr "协方差算子"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A self-adjoint positive-semidefinite linear operator representing centered second moments in a declared real or complex inner-product setting. For finite-dimensional column coordinates with E[‖X‖²] finite, μ = E[X] and C = E[(X-μ)(X-μ)*], where * is conjugate transpose, or ordinary transpose over the reals."
+msgstr "在已声明的实或复内积背景下表示中心二阶矩的自伴半正定线性算子。对于有限维列坐标，若 E[‖X‖²] 有限，则 μ = E[X]，C = E[(X-μ)(X-μ)*]，其中 * 表示共轭转置，在实数情形下为普通转置。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The coordinate formula uses supplied orthonormal bases and the complex convention ⟨u,v⟩ = u* v, conjugate-linear in the first argument. Infinite-dimensional use requires stated existence, boundedness and spectral hypotheses; this type does not assert a discrete eigenvector basis for an arbitrary operator. An unconjugated complex second moment is a different construction."
+msgstr "坐标公式使用已提供的标准正交基以及复内积约定 ⟨u,v⟩ = u* v，第一个变量为共轭线性的。无限维使用需要声明存在性、有界性和谱方面的假设；该类型不声称任意算子都存在离散特征向量基。不带共轭的复二阶矩属于不同构造。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A real random vector equally likely to be (1,0) or (-1,0) has mean zero and covariance diag(1,0) under the standard Euclidean inner product. This covariance is positive semidefinite and singular; its zero eigenvalue is valid, and no inverse is required."
+msgstr "一个以相同概率取 (1,0) 或 (-1,0) 的实随机向量，均值为零，在标准欧氏内积下的协方差为 diag(1,0)。该协方差半正定且奇异；零特征值有效，也不要求存在逆。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified population or empirical covariance operator, retaining the observations or probability model, scalar field, inner product, centering, scaling and actual normalization convention in the source representation."
+msgstr "用于有依据的总体或经验协方差算子，在来源表示中保留观测或概率模型、标量域、内积、中心化、缩放以及实际归一化约定。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer covariance from a Gram-matrix or symmetry label alone, require positive definiteness, or replace a missing operator with zero covariance. Repeated eigenvalues do not select unique eigenvectors. A declared covariance role or solver descriptor does not establish centering, covariance construction or numerical spectral analysis."
+msgstr "不要仅从 Gram 矩阵或对称性标签推断协方差，不要要求正定性，也不要用零协方差代替缺失的算子。重复特征值不选定唯一特征向量。已声明的协方差角色或求解器描述符不能证明已执行中心化、协方差构造或数值谱分析。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/CovarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Retain the inherited LinearMap and Function carrier-set frame separately from the vector-space structure. Use math:covarianceOperator from the analysis to this operator. Preserve sample orientation and divisor: empirical 1/N requires N > 0, while 1/(N-1) requires N > 1. Those choices and their evidence are supplied data, not defaults or new validation gates."
+msgstr "将继承的 LinearMap 和 Function 载体集合框架与向量空间结构分开保留。使用 math:covarianceOperator 从分析关联到此算子。保留样本排列方向和除数：经验约定 1/N 要求 N > 0，而 1/(N-1) 要求 N > 1。这些选择及其依据属于已提供的数据，不是默认值或新的验证关卡。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "covariance operator"
+msgstr "协方差算子"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to the supplied math:CovarianceOperator that is its declared decomposition operand. The analysis process, its input data, the covariance operator and any reported numerical outputs retain separate roles; this link records the operator role rather than constructing it."
+msgstr "将 math:PCAAnalysis 关联到已提供的 math:CovarianceOperator，后者作为其已声明的分解操作数。分析过程、输入数据、协方差算子及任何已报告的数值输出保持不同角色；该链接记录算子角色，而不构造算子。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The current PCA source contract requires at least one covariance-operator resource through its generic minimum and existing closure, associated with math:IncompletePCAAnalysis. This is not an exact-one or typed-target enforcement claim. The mathematical covariance meaning and the inherited operator frame still need their own evidence."
+msgstr "当前 PCA 来源契约通过通用最小基数及现有闭世界闭包要求至少一个协方差算子资源，并关联到 math:IncompletePCAAnalysis。这不意味着已强制恰好一个值或目标类型。协方差的数学含义及继承的算子框架仍各自需要依据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:residualPCA math:covarianceOperator p:residualCovariance and gives that CovarianceOperator domain and codomain p:covSpace. Its fixed Gram, dominant-axis and LDL calculations do not supply observed samples, an executed centering step or a sample-covariance normalization."
+msgstr "exact-pca 生成器输出 p:residualPCA math:covarianceOperator p:residualCovariance，并将该 CovarianceOperator 的定义域和陪域均设为 p:covSpace。其固定 Gram 矩阵、主导轴和 LDL 计算不提供实际观测样本、已执行的中心化步骤或样本协方差归一化。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain the actual covariance operand named by an analysis, together with independently supplied input, preprocessing, scalar-field, inner-product and normalization context."
+msgstr "用于保留分析所命名的实际协方差操作数，以及独立提供的输入、预处理、标量域、内积和归一化上下文。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reverse the analysis-to-operator direction, substitute the dataset or solver for the operator, or infer an executed spectral decomposition from the edge. Missing covariance differs from a supplied operator, which may be zero or singular; no absent operand is repaired by inventing a zero operator or undeclared preprocessing."
+msgstr "不要颠倒从分析到算子的方向，不要用数据集或求解器代替算子，也不要从此边推断已执行谱分解。缺失的协方差不同于已提供的算子，后者可以是零算子或奇异算子；不能通过虚构零算子或未声明的预处理来补全缺失操作数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/covarianceOperator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the analysis to its justified CovarianceOperator resource and preserve that operator’s carrier-set frame and actual construction evidence. Keep centering and scaling declarations on the analysis distinct from proof that those operations ran. The relation supplies no additional maximum, automatic target typing, covariance computation or numerical validation result."
+msgstr "将分析关联到有依据的 CovarianceOperator 资源，并保留该算子的载体集合框架及实际构造依据。将分析上的中心化和缩放声明与这些操作已执行的证明分开。该关系不提供额外的最大基数、自动目标定型、协方差计算或数值验证结果。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Subspace"
+msgstr "线性子空间"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A vector subspace: a subset of a vector space closed under addition and scalar multiplication, itself a math:VectorSpace. A subclass of math:VectorSpace naming the space it sits in through math:subspaceOf. The image of a linear map is a subspace; an arbitrary embedding image or projection residual needs separate subspace justification. A math:OrthogonalComplement is the subspace orthogonal to an operand subspace within a declared inner-product space."
+msgstr "向量子空间：向量空间中对加法和标量乘法封闭的子集，其本身也是 math:VectorSpace。它是 math:VectorSpace 的子类，通过 math:subspaceOf 指明所在空间。线性映射的像是子空间；任意嵌入的像或投影残差需要另行论证其子空间结构。math:OrthogonalComplement 是在已声明的内积空间中与操作数子空间正交的子空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "For W to be a subspace of V over F, W contains zero and uses the induced addition and scalar action of V, closed under every scalar in the same field F. Zero and whole-space subspaces, finite and infinite dimension are allowed. Algebraic closure here does not require topological closedness."
+msgstr "若 W 是域 F 上向量空间 V 的子空间，则 W 包含零向量，使用 V 诱导的加法和标量作用，并对同一域 F 中的每个标量封闭。允许零子空间、整个空间以及有限维和无限维情形。此处的代数封闭性不要求拓扑闭性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "In the real vector space R³ with its usual operations, W = {(x,y,0) : x,y in R} is a subspace, including zero and closed under real linear combinations. The affine plane {(x,y,1) : x,y in R} is not a subspace because it lacks zero."
+msgstr "在使用通常运算的实向量空间 R³ 中，W = {(x,y,0) : x,y 属于 R} 是子空间，包含零向量并对实线性组合封闭。仿射平面 {(x,y,1) : x,y 属于 R} 不是子空间，因为它不包含零向量。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified vector subspace with its ambient vector-space structure and common scalar field retained. A linear-map image or a supplied span can establish a subspace; sampled vectors alone do not establish closure of the sample set."
+msgstr "用于有依据的向量子空间，并保留其环境向量空间结构及共同的标量域。线性映射的像或已提供的线性包可以确立子空间；仅有向量样本并不能确立样本集合的封闭性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer a subspace from an embedding label, a dimension, an arbitrary nonlinear image or residual data. An orthogonal complement requires the declared ambient inner product; a global orthogonal direct-sum decomposition needs its own hypotheses in infinite dimension."
+msgstr "不要从嵌入标签、维数、任意非线性映射的像或残差数据推断子空间。正交补需要已声明的环境内积；在无限维情形中，整个空间的正交直和分解还需要其自身的假设。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Subspace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe W as math:Subspace and link each justified ambient V with math:subspaceOf. Retain math:underlyingSet, math:structureOperation and math:satisfiesAxiom evidence separately from descriptive math:scalarField links. A type or ambient link supplies no automatic closure proof or subspace computation."
+msgstr "将 W 描述为 math:Subspace，并通过 math:subspaceOf 关联到每个有依据的环境空间 V。将 math:underlyingSet、math:structureOperation 和 math:satisfiesAxiom 的依据与描述性的 math:scalarField 链接分开保留。类型或环境链接不提供自动的封闭性证明或子空间计算。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "subspace of"
+msgstr "是其子空间"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:Subspace to the vector space it is a subspace of. Domain math:Subspace, range math:VectorSpace (stated in prose). The ambient space a subspace sits in, and against which its orthogonal complement is taken."
+msgstr "将 math:Subspace 关联到以它为子空间的向量空间。定义域为 math:Subspace，值域为 math:VectorSpace（以文字说明）。该关系指明子空间所在的环境空间，其正交补也在该环境空间中取定。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is W to ambient V, with a common scalar field and induced operations justified separately. Several ambient links may be valid, including W to itself. The source states domain and range in prose without native typing, cardinality, inclusion, transitivity or closure rules for this property."
+msgstr "方向从 W 指向环境空间 V，共同的标量域和诱导运算需另行论证。可以存在多个有效的环境链接，包括 W 指向自身。源定义以文字说明定义域和值域，未为此属性提供原生的类型、基数、包含、传递性或封闭性规则。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The linear-algebra-and-learning example states ex:embeddedSubspace math:subspaceOf ex:complexSpace4096. This records an asserted ambient relationship; the dataset supplies neither an embedding-image link to that subspace nor a proof of linear closure."
+msgstr "linear-algebra-and-learning 示例声明 ex:embeddedSubspace math:subspaceOf ex:complexSpace4096。这记录了一条断言的环境关系；该数据集既未提供从嵌入的像到此子空间的链接，也未提供线性封闭性证明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain each justified ambient vector space of a subspace without choosing a preferred ambient. Preserve the actual scalar-field interpretation and induced operations rather than infer them from shared dimensions or carrier labels."
+msgstr "用于保留子空间的每个有依据的环境向量空间，不选择优先的环境空间。保留实际的标量域解释及诱导运算，而不是从相同维数或载体标签推断它们。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not reverse the relationship, substitute a carrier set or scalar field for the ambient vector-space structure, or treat the edge as a closure certificate. Keep math:orthogonalComplementOf for the operand subspace, math:ambientSpace for its enclosing space and math:definedByInnerProduct for its form; those role referents may coincide."
+msgstr "不要颠倒此关系，用载体集合或标量域替代环境向量空间结构，也不要将此边视为封闭性证明。以 math:orthogonalComplementOf 指明操作数子空间，math:ambientSpace 指明其所在空间，math:definedByInnerProduct 指明其形式；这些角色的指称对象可以重合。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/subspaceOf|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the supplied math:Subspace to its ambient math:VectorSpace and preserve the source justification of zero, addition and same-field scalar closure. For orthogonal-complement descriptions retain the separate operand, ambient and inner-product roles. Neither this edge nor a retrieved competency answer calculates a residual subspace."
+msgstr "将已提供的 math:Subspace 关联到其环境 math:VectorSpace，并保留源中关于零向量、加法及同域标量封闭性的论证。描述正交补时，保留操作数、环境空间和内积的独立角色。此边或检索出的能力问题答案均不计算残差子空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Inner Product Space"
+msgstr "内积空间"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A vector space equipped with an inner product — a math:VectorSpace carrying a math:innerProduct that assigns lengths and angles, so orthogonality and orthogonal complements are defined. A subclass of math:VectorSpace; the complex case carries a math:HermitianInnerProduct. It names the inner product it carries through math:innerProduct."
+msgstr "配备内积的向量空间：带有 math:innerProduct 的 math:VectorSpace，该内积确定长度和角度，使正交性和正交补得以定义。它是 math:VectorSpace 的子类；复数情形带有 math:HermitianInnerProduct。通过 math:innerProduct 指明其配备的内积。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The real case uses a symmetric positive-definite bilinear form; the complex case uses a conjugate-symmetric positive-definite sesquilinear form. Zero dimension, finite and infinite dimension are allowed. Completeness is an additional Hilbert-space condition, not a consequence of this type."
+msgstr "实数情形使用对称正定双线性型；复数情形使用共轭对称的正定半双线性型。允许零维、有限维和无限维情形。完备性是成为希尔伯特空间的额外条件，不是此类型的推论。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "On real R², h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 is an inner product with h(v,v) = v1² + 2 v2², positive for every nonzero v. The coordinate formula presupposes the supplied ordered basis and real scalar interpretation."
+msgstr "在实数空间 R² 上，h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 是内积，且 h(v,v) = v1² + 2 v2² 对每个非零 v 均为正。该坐标公式以已提供的有序基和实标量解释为前提。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when a vector space carries a justified inner product needed for lengths, norms or orthogonality. Retain the space, carrier set, scalar field, coordinate basis and form as separate roles."
+msgstr "用于向量空间带有有依据的内积，且需要描述长度、范数或正交性的情形。保留空间、载体集合、标量域、坐标基和形式的独立角色。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer an inner product from a vector-space, norm or symmetric-matrix label alone, or treat positive-semidefinite or indefinite forms as positive-definite. An angle involving a zero vector is undefined, and complex angle conventions must be stated."
+msgstr "不要仅凭向量空间、范数或对称矩阵标签推断内积，也不要将半正定型或不定型当作正定型。涉及零向量的角度未定义；复数角度约定必须明确说明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/InnerProductSpace|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe the vector-space structure and link its supplied form with math:innerProduct. Keep the inherited carrier, operation and law evidence explicit. A class or form link proves neither the inner-product laws nor completeness and does not invoke the finite real rational numeric core."
+msgstr "描述向量空间结构，并通过 math:innerProduct 关联到已提供的形式。明确保留继承的载体、运算和定律依据。类或形式链接既不证明内积定律或完备性，也不调用有限维实有理数值核心。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Hermitian Inner Product"
+msgstr "厄米内积"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A conjugate-symmetric, positive-definite sesquilinear form on a complex vector space — the inner product ⟨·,·⟩ of the complex case, linear in one argument and conjugate-linear in the other. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject carried by a math:InnerProductSpace through math:innerProduct; it is the structure that defines a math:OrthogonalComplement in the complex (S⊥) case (math:definedByInnerProduct)."
+msgstr "复向量空间上的共轭对称正定半双线性型，即复数情形的内积 ⟨·,·⟩，对一个参数线性，对另一个参数共轭线性。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由 math:InnerProductSpace 通过 math:innerProduct 配备；在复数情形（S⊥）中，它是通过 math:definedByInnerProduct 定义 math:OrthogonalComplement 的结构。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Preserve which argument is conjugate-linear. Under the first-conjugate convention, h(au,bv) = conjugate(a) b h(u,v) and h(v,u) = conjugate(h(u,v)). Positive definiteness requires real h(v,v) > 0 for nonzero v, with h(0,0) = 0."
+msgstr "保留哪个参数为共轭线性的约定。在第一参数共轭线性的约定下，h(au,bv) = conjugate(a) b h(u,v)，且 h(v,u) = conjugate(h(u,v))。正定性要求非零 v 的 h(v,v) 为正实数，并满足 h(0,0) = 0。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "On C with h(z,w) = conjugate(z) w, h(i,1) = -i, h(1,i) = i and h(i,i) = 1. This form is conjugate-linear in the first argument and linear in the second; it is not complex bilinear."
+msgstr "在 C 上取 h(z,w) = conjugate(z) w，则 h(i,1) = -i、h(1,i) = i 且 h(i,i) = 1。该形式对第一参数共轭线性，对第二参数线性；它不是复双线性型。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified positive-definite Hermitian inner product on a complex vector space, retaining its actual scalar field, argument convention and coordinate representation independently."
+msgstr "用于复向量空间上有依据的正定厄米内积，并独立保留其实际标量域、参数约定和坐标表示。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not identify complex sesquilinearity with bilinearity or ordinary symmetry. A Hermitian matrix can be indefinite or positive semidefinite; its label or conjugate symmetry alone does not establish an inner product."
+msgstr "不要将复半双线性等同于双线性或通常的对称性。厄米矩阵可以是不定的或半正定的；仅凭其标签或共轭对称性不能确立内积。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/HermitianInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the form as its own math:HermitianInnerProduct resource. Use math:innerProduct from its space and math:definedByInnerProduct from a complement where applicable. Retain evidence for the laws; these declarations do not execute a complex Hermitian calculation or construct a complement."
+msgstr "将形式命名为独立的 math:HermitianInnerProduct 资源。使用 math:innerProduct 从其空间关联到它，并在适用时使用 math:definedByInnerProduct 从补对象关联到它。保留定律依据；这些声明不执行复厄米计算，也不构造补空间。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "inner product"
+msgstr "内积"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:InnerProductSpace to the inner product it carries — a math:HermitianInnerProduct in the complex case. Domain math:InnerProductSpace, range a math:HermitianInnerProduct or a real inner-product structure (stated in prose). The inner product is what makes orthogonality, and hence a math:OrthogonalComplement, well-defined."
+msgstr "将 math:InnerProductSpace 关联到其配备的内积；复数情形使用 math:HermitianInnerProduct。定义域为 math:InnerProductSpace，值域为 math:HermitianInnerProduct 或实内积结构（以文字说明）。内积使正交性及 math:OrthogonalComplement 得以明确定义。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is space to form. The source states domain and range in prose without a native global functionality or typed-target rule for this property. Several supplied form descriptions do not select a preferred form or establish their equality."
+msgstr "方向从空间指向形式。源定义以文字说明定义域和值域，未为此属性提供原生的全局函数性或目标类型规则。多个已提供的形式描述不会选定优先形式，也不确立它们相等。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real u = (1,1) and v = (1,-1), the standard dot product is zero, while h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 is -1. Linking the intended form matters: the same vectors are orthogonal under one inner product and not the other."
+msgstr "对于实向量 u = (1,1) 和 v = (1,-1)，标准点积为零，而 h(u,v) = u1 v1 + 2 u2 v2 为 -1。关联到所需形式至关重要：相同向量在一个内积下正交，在另一个内积下不正交。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to identify the actual inner product carried by a vector-space description, retaining the real or complex setting and the supplied form laws rather than inferring them from dimensions or labels."
+msgstr "用于指明向量空间描述实际配备的内积，保留实数或复数背景及已提供的形式定律，而不是从维数或标签推断它们。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute a scalar pairing result, coordinate matrix, basis or residual for the form. The edge neither transforms coordinates nor proves symmetry, sesquilinearity or positive definiteness."
+msgstr "不要用标量配对结果、坐标矩阵、基或残差替代形式。此边既不变换坐标，也不证明对称性、半双线性或正定性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/innerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Point math:innerProduct from the space to its supplied form resource. Preserve the carrier, scalar field, basis and argument convention separately. Retain each justified description without a preferred-form rule; a link does not invoke a numerical evaluator."
+msgstr "使用 math:innerProduct 从空间指向其已提供的形式资源。分别保留载体、标量域、基和参数约定。保留每个有依据的描述，不设优先形式规则；链接不会调用数值求值器。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "defined by inner product"
+msgstr "由内积定义"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:OrthogonalComplement to the inner product that defines orthogonality for it — the math:HermitianInnerProduct in the complex case. Domain math:OrthogonalComplement, range a math:HermitianInnerProduct or real inner-product structure (stated in prose). An orthogonal complement without a named inner product is ambiguous and ill-formed (math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement)."
+msgstr "将 math:OrthogonalComplement 关联到定义其正交性的内积；复数情形使用 math:HermitianInnerProduct。定义域为 math:OrthogonalComplement，值域为 math:HermitianInnerProduct 或实内积结构（以文字说明）。未指明内积的正交补含义不明且结构不完整（math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement）。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The existing OrthogonalComplement-local source profile has minimum one, maximum one and all-values restrictions with logic:Thing, plus required-path closure and the associated math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement diagnostic. This generic resource contract does not prove that the target is a positive-definite Hermitian form."
+msgstr "现有仅针对 OrthogonalComplement 的源配置具有以 logic:Thing 为限定的最少一个、最多一个及所有值限制，并有必需路径闭包和相应诊断 math:UnqualifiedOrthogonalComplement。这一通用资源契约不证明目标是正定厄米型。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The ordinary linear-algebra-and-learning example states ex:residualSubspace math:definedByInnerProduct ex:hermitianInnerProduct, separately from its operand and ambient links. This names a defining form without evaluating it or proving the complement equation."
+msgstr "普通 linear-algebra-and-learning 示例声明 ex:residualSubspace math:definedByInnerProduct ex:hermitianInnerProduct，并另行声明操作数和环境链接。这指明了定义形式，但不对其求值，也不证明补空间等式。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when an orthogonal-complement description needs to retain the actual form defining orthogonality within its declared ambient space. Keep that form consistent with the supplied mathematical construction and argument convention."
+msgstr "用于正交补描述需要保留在其已声明环境空间中定义正交性的实际形式的情形。该形式须与已提供的数学构造及参数约定一致。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not confuse the complement-to-form direction with math:innerProduct from the ambient space. The class-local restriction is not global property functionality, automatic Hermitian target typing or proof that every complement vector is orthogonal to the operand."
+msgstr "不要将从补对象到形式的方向与从环境空间出发的 math:innerProduct 混淆。类局部限制不是全局属性函数性、自动厄米目标类型推断，也不证明补空间中每个向量均与操作数正交。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/definedByInnerProduct|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the complement to its supplied form and retain math:orthogonalComplementOf, math:ambientSpace and math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement separately. Those roles need not have distinct referents. The competency query retrieves declarations; mathematical justification and computation remain separate evidence."
+msgstr "将补对象关联到其已提供的形式，并分别保留 math:orthogonalComplementOf、math:ambientSpace 和 math:complementSemantics math:orthogonalComplement。这些角色的指称对象不必不同。能力问题查询检索声明；数学论证和计算仍须作为独立依据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Explained Variance"
+msgstr "解释方差"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The share of positive finite total variance accounted for by a math:PrincipalComponent: its nonnegative covariance eigenvalue divided by the covariance trace, a dimensionless ratio in [0, 1]. A zero total variance leaves the ratio undefined. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:explainedVarianceRatio; the ratios across retained components quantify retained variance."
+msgstr "math:PrincipalComponent 所占的正且有限的总方差份额：将其非负协方差特征值除以协方差迹，得到 [0, 1] 中的无量纲比率。总方差为零时，该比率未定义。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由 PCA 通过 math:explainedVarianceRatio 命名；各保留分量的比率量化保留的方差。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This class records a normalized per-component share, distinct from an unnormalized variance amount. Finite covariance matrices use their trace as total variance. Infinite-dimensional use needs justified finite-trace spectral assumptions; no complete eigenbasis follows from this type."
+msgstr "此类记录归一化的单分量份额，与未归一化的方差量不同。有限维协方差矩阵以其迹作为总方差。无限维用法需要有依据的有限迹谱假设；此类型不蕴含完整特征基。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For covariance diag(3,1,0), total variance is 4 and the associated component ratios are 3/4, 1/4 and 0. Retaining only the first component retains 3/4 of total variance. Zero covariance instead gives an undefined ratio, not a ratio of zero."
+msgstr "对于协方差 diag(3,1,0)，总方差为 4，对应分量的比率为 3/4、1/4 和 0。仅保留第一分量可保留总方差的 3/4。零协方差则产生未定义的比率，而不是零比率。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a supplied component share justified by its nonnegative covariance eigenvalue and positive finite total variance. Preserve the actual covariance, scalar field, basis, preprocessing and normalization evidence together with the source component association."
+msgstr "用于已提供的分量份额，其依据为非负协方差特征值及正且有限的总方差。保留实际协方差、标量域、基、预处理和归一化依据，以及源中的分量对应关系。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace missing data or zero-total undefined normalization with zero or one. A ratio sum of one can omit zero-variance components and does not prove a complete basis, semantic importance or predictive quality. Retained variance and cumulative shares are separate claims."
+msgstr "不要将缺失数据或因总量为零而未定义的归一化替换为零或一。比率之和为一时仍可能遗漏零方差分量，不能证明基的完整性、语义重要性或预测质量。保留方差与累计份额是不同的声明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExplainedVariance|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the result as math:ExplainedVariance and link it from the analysis with math:explainedVarianceRatio. Preserve its supplied magnitude, component association, order and multiplicity in the existing source representation. A descriptor alone supplies no numeric value or normalization computation."
+msgstr "将结果命名为 math:ExplainedVariance，并通过 math:explainedVarianceRatio 从分析关联到它。在现有源表示中保留已提供的数值大小、分量对应关系、顺序和重数。单独的描述符不提供数值或归一化计算。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "explained variance ratio"
+msgstr "解释方差比率"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:ExplainedVariance it produces — the share of total variance a component accounts for. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:ExplainedVariance (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "将 math:PCAAnalysis 关联到它产生的 math:ExplainedVariance，即某分量所占的总方差份额。定义域为 math:PCAAnalysis，值域为 math:ExplainedVariance（以文字说明）。它是分析声明的一项输出。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The property signature is stated in prose. The existing PCA-local profile has a generic logic:Thing minimum and all-values restriction plus required-path closure, without a dedicated maximum, typed-target rule or numeric denominator/range proof."
+msgstr "属性签名以文字说明。现有仅针对 PCA 的配置具有通用 logic:Thing 最小数量及所有值限制，并有必需路径闭包，但没有专用的最大数量、目标类型规则或数值分母及范围证明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact-pca producer emits p:residualPCA math:explainedVarianceRatio p:pc1Variance and types that descriptor as math:ExplainedVariance. Its fixed Gram, dominant-axis and LDL results supply neither a numeric ratio nor a PCA eigenvalue family."
+msgstr "exact-pca 生成器输出 p:residualPCA math:explainedVarianceRatio p:pc1Variance，并将该描述符标为 math:ExplainedVariance。其固定 Gram 矩阵、主导轴和 LDL 结果既不提供数值比率，也不提供 PCA 特征值族。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain a justified normalized component-result resource declared by a PCA analysis. Keep the source evidence identifying its actual component, covariance and normalization context independently of the other output relations."
+msgstr "用于保留 PCA 分析声明的、有依据的归一化分量结果资源。将源中识别其实际分量、协方差和归一化背景的依据与其他输出关系独立保留。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not substitute a literal, eigenvalue amount or singular value for this result resource. Unordered component and variance links do not establish pairings. The current competency query joins those roles independently; its rows are not numeric association certificates."
+msgstr "不要用字面量、未归一化特征值或奇异值替代此结果资源。无序的分量和方差链接不能确立配对。当前能力问题查询独立连接这些角色；其结果行不是数值对应关系的证明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/explainedVarianceRatio|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Point the property from the analysis to the supplied math:ExplainedVariance resource. Preserve its actual source value and component association without inferring order, repeated occurrences or a default ratio. The link alone performs no normalization or numeric validation."
+msgstr "使用此属性从分析指向已提供的 math:ExplainedVariance 资源。保留其实际源值和分量对应关系，不推断顺序、重复出现次数或默认比率。此链接本身不执行归一化或数值验证。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Principal Component"
+msgstr "主成分"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A principal component: one orthonormal direction of maximal remaining variance produced by a math:PCAAnalysis — an eigenvector of the math:CovarianceOperator. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject, named by an analysis through math:principalComponent, carrying a math:LoadingVector (its coefficients) and explaining a share of variance (math:ExplainedVariance). Its MEANING is never an intrinsic property: what a component encodes is a math:ResidualInterpretationClaim held from a vantage."
+msgstr "一个主成分：math:PCAAnalysis 产生的正交归一方向之一，在剩余方向中具有最大方差——即 math:CovarianceOperator 的特征向量。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由分析通过 math:principalComponent 命名，带有 math:LoadingVector（其系数），并解释一部分方差（math:ExplainedVariance）。其含义绝不是固有属性：某个成分编码什么，是从一个立场持有的 math:ResidualInterpretationClaim。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "GMEOW uses the direction convention: a normalized nonzero covariance eigenvector in a declared geometry. The PCA review also uses component for a linear combination of variables. Keep that score-variable usage distinct from this direction and its LoadingVector coefficient representation; these roles impose no class disjointness or resource inequality."
+msgstr "GMEOW 采用方向约定：在已声明几何结构中的归一化非零协方差特征向量。PCA 综述也用成分指变量的线性组合。应将这种得分变量用法与这里的方向及其 LoadingVector 系数表示区分开；这些角色不施加类不相交或资源不相等要求。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For real covariance diag(3,1,0) in the standard Euclidean basis, the coordinate directions have eigenvalues 3, 1 and 0. The third unit direction is still a valid component direction; its zero eigenvalue does not make the vector zero."
+msgstr "对于标准欧氏基下的实协方差 diag(3,1,0)，各坐标方向的特征值分别为 3、1 和 0。第三个单位方向仍是有效的成分方向；其零特征值不会使向量变成零向量。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for a justified PCA output direction, retaining the covariance, scalar field, inner product, preprocessing, normalization and selected component family in the source evidence."
+msgstr "用于有依据的 PCA 输出方向，并在源证据中保留协方差、标量域、内积、预处理、归一化及所选成分族。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer semantic importance, computed scores or a unique preferred direction from this type. Repeated eigenvalues permit different eigenspace bases, sign or complex phase choices persist, and a truncated family need not span the input. Zero dimension supplies no nonzero component."
+msgstr "不要从此类型推断语义重要性、已计算的得分或唯一优先方向。重复特征值允许特征空间采用不同的基，符号或复相位选择仍然存在，截断成分族未必张成输入空间。零维空间不提供非零成分。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/PrincipalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Link the analysis through math:principalComponent and retain ordered component and coefficient associations in the source representation. Keep any interpretation in a vantage-bearing math:ResidualInterpretationClaim; an output descriptor alone proves neither orthonormality nor an executed eigendecomposition."
+msgstr "通过 math:principalComponent 从分析建立链接，并在源表示中保留有序成分及系数关联。将任何解释放在带有立场的 math:ResidualInterpretationClaim 中；仅有输出描述符既不能证明正交归一性，也不能证明已执行特征分解。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "principal component"
+msgstr "主成分"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to one of the math:PrincipalComponent directions it produces. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:PrincipalComponent (stated in prose). The declared component outputs; a PCA producing none is ill-formed (math:IncompletePCAAnalysis)."
+msgstr "将 math:PCAAnalysis 关联到它产生的一个 math:PrincipalComponent 方向。定义域为 math:PCAAnalysis，值域为 math:PrincipalComponent（以文字说明）。这是已声明的成分输出；不产生任何成分的 PCA 是结构不完整的（math:IncompletePCAAnalysis）。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This analysis-to-direction relation has a prose-only signature. The PCA-local generic Thing minimum, all-values restriction and required-path closure supply no dedicated maximum, automatic PrincipalComponent target typing, numerical normalization or variance ordering."
+msgstr "这个从分析指向方向的关系只有文字说明的签名。PCA 局部针对通用 Thing 的最小数量限制、所有值限制和必需路径闭包，不提供专用最大数量、自动 PrincipalComponent 目标类型标注、数值归一化或方差排序。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "An analysis can declare two supplied directions through math:principalComponent. The two unordered links retain those output roles without saying which has greater variance or which loading and score resources belong to either direction."
+msgstr "一个分析可以通过 math:principalComponent 声明两个已提供的方向。这两个无序链接保留其输出角色，但不说明哪个方向方差更大，也不说明哪些载荷和得分资源属于其中任一方向。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to record the principal directions that a supplied PCA reports, preserving their identities and the actual field, covariance and component-selection evidence."
+msgstr "用于记录所提供 PCA 报告的主方向，保留它们的身份以及实际标量域、协方差和成分选择证据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not treat resource counts, IRI names or repeated RDF assertions as component rank, multiplicity, ordering or a complete basis. Missing directions are not zero directions; never invent a component merely to fill the required role."
+msgstr "不要将资源计数、IRI 名称或重复 RDF 断言视为成分排名、重数、顺序或完整基。缺失方向不是零方向；绝不为填充必需角色而虚构成分。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/principalComponent|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Keep math:loadingVector, math:scoreVector and math:explainedVarianceRatio as separate analysis-output roles, with their actual associations retained in the source. The current competency query joins components and variance descriptors independently; its IRI ordering establishes no numeric pairing."
+msgstr "将 math:loadingVector、math:scoreVector 和 math:explainedVarianceRatio 保留为独立的分析输出角色，并在源中保留其实际关联。当前能力查询分别连接成分与方差描述符；其中的 IRI 排序不建立数值配对。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Loading Vector"
+msgstr "载荷向量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A loading vector: the coefficients of a math:PrincipalComponent in the original coordinates — how each input feature contributes to the component. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:loadingVector. Loadings are the eigenvectors of the math:CovarianceOperator; their INTERPRETATION is a math:ResidualInterpretationClaim, not an intrinsic property."
+msgstr "一个载荷向量：math:PrincipalComponent 在原始坐标中的系数——各输入特征对该成分的贡献。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由 PCA 通过 math:loadingVector 命名。载荷是 math:CovarianceOperator 的特征向量；其解释是 math:ResidualInterpretationClaim，而不是固有属性。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This is the coefficient-vector convention: the coordinates of a component direction in a supplied ordered feature basis for the prepared input. Retain the normalization convention; a coordinate representation is distinct from the geometric direction without requiring different RDF resources."
+msgstr "这里采用系数向量约定：在针对已预处理输入所提供的有序特征基下，一个成分方向的坐标。应保留归一化约定；坐标表示与几何方向是不同角色，但不要求使用不同的 RDF 资源。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "In the standard real basis, a component with loading coefficients (1,0,0) selects the first prepared feature. The zero entries are valid coefficients of a nonzero unit vector; they are not missing data or zero-variance conclusions."
+msgstr "在标准实数基下，载荷系数为 (1,0,0) 的成分选取第一个已预处理特征。其中的零值是非零单位向量的有效系数；它们既不是缺失数据，也不是零方差结论。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for supplied component coefficients with feature identities, basis order, field, units, centering/scaling and normalization evidence. Coefficients in standardized features are not automatically coefficients in unprocessed physical units."
+msgstr "用于已提供的成分系数，并保留特征身份、基顺序、标量域、单位、中心化/缩放及归一化证据。标准化特征中的系数不会自动成为未经处理的物理单位下的系数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not silently substitute correlation-scaled loadings, biplot markers, factor-analysis loadings or importance scores. Correlation needs nonzero feature and component-score variances; a zero eigenvalue leaves the corresponding correlation undefined, not zero. A zero feature scale licenses no division."
+msgstr "不要悄然替换为按相关性缩放的载荷、双标图标记、因子分析载荷或重要性得分。相关性要求特征方差和成分得分方差均非零；零特征值使相应相关性无定义，而不是为零。特征尺度为零不允许进行除法。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/LoadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Name the supplied result from its analysis with math:loadingVector and retain component/feature associations and any coordinate transformation in the source representation. Changes of sign, phase or tied-eigenspace basis require consistent score coordinates; interpretation remains a vantage-bearing claim."
+msgstr "从分析通过 math:loadingVector 命名所提供的结果，并在源表示中保留成分/特征关联和任何坐标变换。符号、相位或重复特征值所对应特征空间的基发生变化时，得分坐标必须一致地变化；解释仍是带有立场的主张。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "loading vector"
+msgstr "载荷向量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:LoadingVector it produces — the coefficients of a component in the original features. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:LoadingVector (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "将 math:PCAAnalysis 关联到它产生的 math:LoadingVector——一个成分在原始特征中的系数。定义域为 math:PCAAnalysis，值域为 math:LoadingVector（以文字说明）。这是分析的一项已声明输出。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The direction is analysis to coefficient resource. Its signature is stated in prose; the generic PCA-local Thing minimum, all-values restriction and closure establish no typed target, dedicated maximum, coordinate length or component-to-loading pairing."
+msgstr "方向是从分析指向系数资源。其签名以文字说明；PCA 局部针对通用 Thing 的最小数量限制、所有值限制和闭包，不建立目标类型、专用最大数量、坐标长度或成分与载荷之间的配对。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The exact Gram/PCA producer links its analysis to pc1Loadings and types that descriptor math:LoadingVector. It supplies no numeric loading coefficients, so the declaration is not evidence that a covariance eigenvector was computed."
+msgstr "精确 Gram/PCA 生成器将分析链接到 pc1Loadings，并将该描述符标注为 math:LoadingVector。它不提供数值载荷系数，因此该声明不能证明已计算协方差特征向量。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to retain identified loading outputs of the stated analysis, alongside the source's component, feature-order, preprocessing and coefficient-normalization context."
+msgstr "用于保留所述分析中已标识的载荷输出，以及源中的成分、特征顺序、预处理和系数归一化上下文。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not infer one loading per component, an ordered association or a numeric payload from link counts or matching resource names. This relation does not compute coefficients or convert correlation-scaled loadings into the selected coefficient convention."
+msgstr "不要从链接计数或资源名称对应推断每个成分恰有一个载荷、存在有序关联或存在数值载荷内容。这个关系既不计算系数，也不将按相关性缩放的载荷转换为所选系数约定。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/loadingVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Describe a justified LoadingVector result and preserve its supplied coordinates and associations through the existing source representation. Retain the actual input transformation and its scale conditions; neither a link nor a policy label performs centering, scaling or spectral analysis."
+msgstr "描述有依据的 LoadingVector 结果，并通过现有源表示保留其已提供的坐标与关联。应保留实际输入变换及其尺度条件；链接和策略标签都不执行中心化、缩放或谱分析。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Score Vector"
+msgstr "得分向量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A score vector: the coordinates of a data point projected onto the principal components — the representation of a sample in the PCA basis. A subclass of math:MathematicalObject named by a PCA through math:scoreVector. Scores are inputs projected through the loadings."
+msgstr "一个得分向量：一个数据点投影到各主成分所得的坐标——一个样本在 PCA 基下的表示。它是 math:MathematicalObject 的子类，由 PCA 通过 math:scoreVector 命名。得分是输入通过载荷投影所得的结果。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "GMEOW uses one sample's tuple across retained components. A component's scores across samples are a different view of the score matrix. Preserve sample identity and component order; neither this role nor the loading/direction roles imply global class disjointness."
+msgstr "GMEOW 使用一个样本在保留成分上的坐标元组。一个成分在各样本上的得分是得分矩阵的另一种视图。应保留样本身份和成分顺序；此角色与载荷/方向角色都不蕴含全局类不相交。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "For prepared real sample (2,-1,4) and ordered loading columns (1,0,0) and (0,1,0), the sample score tuple is (2,-1). It retains two projection coordinates, not the omitted third coordinate or a complete reconstruction."
+msgstr "对于已预处理的实数样本 (2,-1,4)，若有序载荷列为 (1,0,0) 和 (0,1,0)，该样本的得分元组为 (2,-1)。它保留两个投影坐标，不保留被省略的第三个坐标，也不构成完整重建。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use for supplied coordinates of an identified sample in a declared retained PCA frame, keeping its input transformation, field, geometry, component order and projection evidence."
+msgstr "用于一个已标识样本在已声明的保留 PCA 坐标框架中的已提供坐标，并保留输入变换、标量域、几何结构、成分顺序及投影证据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not read scores as nonnegative variance ratios, loading coefficients or semantic importance. Zero tuples and negative entries can be valid. A zero score tuple is not an invalid zero eigenvector, and a truncated tuple need not recover the input."
+msgstr "不要将得分理解为非负方差比例、载荷系数或语义重要性。零元组和负数条目可以是有效的。零得分元组不是无效的零特征向量，截断元组也未必能恢复输入。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ScoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "In a finite real Euclidean convention with prepared observation rows X and ordered loading columns A, T = X A has sample tuples in rows and one component's scores in each column. Retain those associations in the source; complex or other geometries need their actual conjugation and inner-product conventions."
+msgstr "在有限维实欧氏约定下，若 X 的行是已预处理的观测，A 的列是有序载荷，则 T = X A 的行是样本元组，每列是一个成分的得分。应在源中保留这些关联；复数或其他几何结构需要其实际共轭和内积约定。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "score vector"
+msgstr "得分向量"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "Relates a math:PCAAnalysis to a math:ScoreVector it produces — a data point's coordinates in the principal-component basis. Domain math:PCAAnalysis, range math:ScoreVector (stated in prose). A declared output of the analysis."
+msgstr "将 math:PCAAnalysis 关联到它产生的 math:ScoreVector——一个数据点在主成分基下的坐标。定义域为 math:PCAAnalysis，值域为 math:ScoreVector（以文字说明）。这是分析的一项已声明输出。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This links an analysis to a supplied sample-coordinate resource, not a numeric literal. Its prose-only signature and PCA-local generic Thing minimum, all-values restriction and closure establish no typed target, dedicated maximum, sample association or tuple-dimension proof."
+msgstr "此属性将分析链接到已提供的样本坐标资源，而不是数值字面量。仅以文字说明的签名和 PCA 局部针对通用 Thing 的最小数量限制、所有值限制及闭包，不建立目标类型、专用最大数量、样本关联或元组维度证明。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "The ordinary scene names sampleScores through math:scoreVector and types it math:ScoreVector. It gives no numeric tuple or sample-association structure; the resource name alone does not supply either."
+msgstr "普通场景通过 math:scoreVector 命名 sampleScores，并将其标注为 math:ScoreVector。它既不提供数值元组，也不提供样本关联结构；仅靠资源名称不能补出其中任一项。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to catalogue supplied sample-score outputs of the declared analysis, retaining each sample identity, component-position correspondence and preprocessing/projection context in the source evidence."
+msgstr "用于编目已声明分析中已提供的样本得分输出，并在源证据中保留各样本身份、成分位置对应及预处理/投影上下文。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Do not replace absent scores with zero tuples or infer that all samples were projected. This output link and the producer's Gram/LDL calculations do not compute sample scores or establish feature/component pairing."
+msgstr "不要以零元组替换缺失得分，也不要推断所有样本都已投影。这个输出链接和生成器的 Gram/LDL 计算既不计算样本得分，也不建立特征/成分配对。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/scoreVector|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Keep the result linked from its analysis and retain its actual sample, ordered components, coefficient representation and prepared input together in the source. The current competency query retrieves component and variance roles without retrieving or validating score coordinates."
+msgstr "保持从分析到结果的链接，并在源中一同保留其实际样本、有序成分、系数表示和已预处理输入。当前能力查询提取成分与方差角色，但不提取或验证得分坐标。"
diff --git slices/grounding/math/mappings/equivalences.ttl slices/grounding/math/mappings/equivalences.ttl
index 9657d9546..6155a3f2a 100644
--- slices/grounding/math/mappings/equivalences.ttl
+++ slices/grounding/math/mappings/equivalences.ttl
@@ -2209,11 +2209,14 @@ math:TangentSpace skos:relatedMatch <https://leanprover-community.github.io/math
 # External anchors to Wikidata (identity where the concept coincides, closeMatch
 # where GMEOW's object is a facet of a broader concept). Every QID curl-validated by
 # sense (HTTP 200 + English label match). The decomposition/latent/tensor terms with
-# no external concept — math:LatentSpace, math:EmbeddingDimension, math:ScoreVector,
+# no selected external correspondence — math:LatentSpace, math:EmbeddingDimension, math:ScoreVector,
 # math:LoadingVector, math:ProjectionResidual, math:ResidualInterpretationClaim,
 # math:TensorComputationGraph, math:ParameterSpace, math:WeightTensor,
-# math:CovarianceOperator, math:AttentionOperation — are GMEOW-original and are left
-# unanchored rather than aligned to an approximate match. The OpenMath eigen content
+# math:AttentionOperation — are left unanchored rather than aligned to an
+# unsupported match. This mapping choice asserts neither mathematical novelty
+# nor the absence of an external concept.
+# math:CovarianceOperator has a validation-only conceptual close match below.
+# The OpenMath eigen content
 # dictionary (linalgeig) does not resolve, so eigen alignment rides Wikidata alone.
 
 math:InnerProductSpace skos:exactMatch wd:Q214159 {|
@@ -2272,6 +2275,19 @@ math:LinearMap skos:exactMatch wd:Q207643 {|
     logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation
 |} .
 
+math:CovarianceOperator skos:closeMatch wd:Q5178900 {|
